<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<usx version="3.1">
<book code="JOB" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">Job</para>

<para style="toc1">Job</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="JOB 1"/>

<para style="s">Job’s Character and Wealth</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 1:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">James 5:7–12</char></note>There was a man in the land of Uz—Job <char style="add">was</char> his name—and that man was blameless and upright and fearing God and turning away from evil. <verse eid="JOB 1:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 1:2"/>And there were born to him seven sons and three daughters. <verse eid="JOB 1:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 1:3"/>And his possessions were seven thousand sheep, and three thousand camels, and five hundred pair of oxen, and five hundred female donkeys, and a very large service. And that man was greater than all the sons of the East. <verse eid="JOB 1:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 1:4"/>And his sons would go and make a feast <char style="add">at</char> the house of each man <char style="add">in</char> his day, and they would send and call to their three sisters to eat and to drink with them. <verse eid="JOB 1:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 1:5"/>And it came to pass that the days of the feasting had gone around, and Job would send and would sanctify them, and he would rise early in the morning and offer up burnt offerings, the number of them all, for Job said, “Perhaps my sons have sinned and cursed God in their hearts.” Thus Job did all the days. <verse eid="JOB 1:5"/></para>

<para style="s">Satan’s First Attack</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 1:6"/>And there was a day when the sons of God came to present themselves before YHWH, that Satan<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Accuser</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Adversary</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; here and throughout Job 1</char></note> also came into their midst. <verse eid="JOB 1:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 1:7"/>And YHWH said to Satan, “From where have you come?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="JOB 1:7">And Satan answered YHWH and said, “From roaming on the earth, and walking back and forth on it.” <verse eid="JOB 1:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 1:8"/>And YHWH said to Satan, “Have you set your heart upon My servant Job, how there is no one like him on the earth, a man blameless and upright, fearing God and turning aside from evil?” <verse eid="JOB 1:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 1:9"/>And Satan answered YHWH and said, “Does Job fear God for nothing? <verse eid="JOB 1:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 1:10"/>Have you not put a hedge around him and around his house, and around all that <char style="add">is</char> unto him, surrounding <char style="add">on every side</char>? The work of his hands You have blessed, and the <char style="add">animals of</char> his possession have burst forth in the land. <verse eid="JOB 1:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 1:11"/>But now stretch out Your hand and touch against all that <char style="add">is</char> unto him, if he will not curse you to your face!” <verse eid="JOB 1:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 1:12"/>And YHWH said to Satan, “Behold, all that <char style="add">is</char> unto him <char style="add">is</char> in your hand; only against him do not stretch out your hand.” </para>

<para style="p" vid="JOB 1:12">And Satan went out from the face of YHWH. <verse eid="JOB 1:12"/></para>

<para style="s">Job Loses His Children and Possessions</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 1:13"/>And there came to be a day when his sons and his daughters <char style="add">were</char> eating and drinking wine in the house of their brother, the firstborn. <verse eid="JOB 1:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 1:14"/>And a messenger came to Job and said, “The oxen were plowing and the donkeys were grazing at their sides, <verse eid="JOB 1:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 1:15"/>when the Sabeans fell on them and took them, and they struck the servants with the mouth of the sword—and only I have escaped, by myself alone, to declare <char style="add">it</char> to you.” <verse eid="JOB 1:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 1:16"/>Still this one was speaking, when this one came and said, “The fire of God fell from the heavens and burned up the sheep and the servants, and it consumed them—and only I have escaped, by myself alone, to declare <char style="add">it</char> to you.” <verse eid="JOB 1:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 1:17"/>Still this one was speaking, when this one came and said, “The Chaldeans made three heads and rushed upon the camels and took them away, and they struck the servants with the mouth of the sword—and only I have escaped, by myself alone, to declare <char style="add">it</char> to you.” <verse eid="JOB 1:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 1:18"/>Still this one was speaking, when this one came and said, “Your sons and daughters <char style="add">were</char> eating and drinking wine in the house of their brother, the firstborn, <verse eid="JOB 1:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 1:19"/>and behold, a great wind came from across the desert and struck against the four corners of the house, and it fell upon the young people, and they died—and only I have escaped, by myself alone, to declare <char style="add">it</char> to you.” <verse eid="JOB 1:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 1:20"/>And Job arose and tore his robe and shaved his head, and he fell to the ground and bowed low, <verse eid="JOB 1:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 1:21"/>and he said, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 1:21">“Naked I came forth from the womb of my mother, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 1:21">and naked I shall return there. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 1:21">YHWH gave, and YHWH has taken away. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 1:21">Let the name of YHWH be blessed.” <verse eid="JOB 1:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 1:22"/>In all this Job did not sin, and he did not ascribe foolishness to God. <verse eid="JOB 1:22"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 1"/>

<chapter number="2" style="c" sid="JOB 2"/>

<para style="s">Job Loses His Health</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 2:1"/>And there was a day when the sons of God came to present themselves before YHWH, and Satan<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Accuser</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Adversary</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; here and throughout Job 2</char></note> also came into their midst to present himself before YHWH. <verse eid="JOB 2:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 2:2"/>And YHWH said to Satan, “From where have you come to here?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="JOB 2:2">And Satan answered YHWH and said, “From roaming on the earth and walking back and forth on it.” <verse eid="JOB 2:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 2:3"/>And YHWH said to Satan, “Have you set your heart toward My servant Job, how there is no one like him on the earth, a man complete and upright, fearing God and turning aside from evil? And still he holds firmly to his integrity, although you incited Me against him to devour him without cause.” <verse eid="JOB 2:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 2:4"/>But Satan answered YHWH and said, “Skin for skin—and all that <char style="add">is</char> unto the man, he will give for his life. <verse eid="JOB 2:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 2:5"/>But now stretch out Your hand and touch upon his bone and upon his flesh—if he will not curse You to Your face!” <verse eid="JOB 2:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 2:6"/>And YHWH said to Satan, “Behold, he <char style="add">is</char> in your hand, yet his life you must spare.” <verse eid="JOB 2:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 2:7"/>And Satan went forth from the face of YHWH, and he struck Job with severe boils from the sole of his foot even up to the crown of his head. <verse eid="JOB 2:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 2:8"/>And he took for himself a potsherd to scrape himself with it, and he was sitting in the midst of the ashes. <verse eid="JOB 2:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 2:9"/>And his wife said to him, “Are you still holding firmly onto your integrity? Curse<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Bless</char></note> God and die!” <verse eid="JOB 2:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 2:10"/>And he said to her, “You speak like the speaking of one of the foolish women! Shall we receive the good from God, and not also receive the bad?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="JOB 2:10">In all this, Job did not sin with his lips. <verse eid="JOB 2:10"/></para>

<para style="s">Job’s Three Friends</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 2:11"/>And three friends of Job heard of all this evil that had come upon him, and they came, each man from his place—Eliphaz the Temanite, and Bildad the Shuhite, and Zophar the Naamathite—and they met together to come to nod to him and to comfort him. <verse eid="JOB 2:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 2:12"/>And they lifted their eyes from afar, and they did not recognize him. And they lifted their voices and wept, and each man tore his robe, and they scattered dust upon their heads toward the heavens. <verse eid="JOB 2:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 2:13"/>Then they sat down with him on the ground seven days and seven nights, and there was no speaking to him a word, for they saw that <char style="add">his</char> pain was very great. <verse eid="JOB 2:13"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 2"/>

<chapter number="3" style="c" sid="JOB 3"/>

<para style="s">Job Laments His Birth</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 3:1"/>After this, Job opened his mouth and cursed his day. <verse eid="JOB 3:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 3:2"/>And Job spoke and said: <verse eid="JOB 3:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 3:3"/>“May the day perish on which I was born, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:3">and the night <char style="add">that</char> one said, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:3">‘A male child has been conceived.’ <verse eid="JOB 3:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 3:4"/>That day—may it be darkness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:4">let not God seek it above, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:4">nor let light shine upon it. <verse eid="JOB 3:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 3:5"/>Let darkness and the shadow of death claim it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:5">may a cloud dwell over it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:5">let the blackness of the day terrify it. <verse eid="JOB 3:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 3:6"/>That night—let darkness take it! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:6">Let it not it rejoice among the days of the year; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:6">into the number of the months let it not come. <verse eid="JOB 3:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 3:7"/>Behold, that night—may it be barren, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:7">let no joyful shout come into it. <verse eid="JOB 3:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 3:8"/>May they curse it, those cursing the day,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">cursing the sea</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:8">those ready to rouse Leviathan. <verse eid="JOB 3:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 3:9"/>May the stars of its morning light be dark; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:9">may it look for light and there <char style="add">be</char> none, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:9">and do not let it see the eyelids of the dawn; <verse eid="JOB 3:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 3:10"/>for it did not shut the doors of my womb, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:10">and hide trouble from my eyes. <verse eid="JOB 3:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 3:11"/>Why did I not die from the womb? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:11">I should have come forth from the belly and expired! <verse eid="JOB 3:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 3:12"/>Why did the knees meet me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:12">and why the breasts that I should suck? <verse eid="JOB 3:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 3:13"/>For now I would have lain down and been quiet; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:13">I would have slept—then there would be rest for me <verse eid="JOB 3:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 3:14"/>with the kings and counselors of the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:14">who built <char style="add">up</char> ruins for themselves; <verse eid="JOB 3:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 3:15"/>or with the princes <char style="add">with</char> gold unto them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:15">those filling their houses <char style="add">with</char> silver. <verse eid="JOB 3:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 3:16"/>Or <char style="add">why</char> was I not hidden like a stillborn child, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:16">like infants <char style="add">who</char> had not seen the light? <verse eid="JOB 3:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 3:17"/>There the wicked cease <char style="add">from</char> trouble, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:17">and there those weary of power are at rest— <verse eid="JOB 3:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 3:18"/>together the captives are at rest; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:18">they do not hear the voice oppressing <char style="add">them</char>. <verse eid="JOB 3:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 3:19"/>The small and the great there the same, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:19">and the servant <char style="add">is</char> free from his master. <verse eid="JOB 3:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 3:20"/>Why is light given to the one toiling, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:20">and life to the bitter of soul, <verse eid="JOB 3:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 3:21"/>those waiting for death and there is none, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:21">and those digging for it more than hidden treasures, <verse eid="JOB 3:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 3:22"/>those being glad unto joy; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:22">they rejoice that they should find the grave? <verse eid="JOB 3:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 3:23"/>To a man <char style="add">for</char> whom his path is hidden, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:23">and God has hedged around him? <verse eid="JOB 3:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 3:24"/>For before my food my sighing comes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:24">and my groanings pour out like the waters. <verse eid="JOB 3:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 3:25"/>For the dreadful thing I dreaded, and it has met me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:25">and that which I had feared has come to me. <verse eid="JOB 3:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 3:26"/>I am not at ease, nor am I quiet; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 3:26">and I do not have rest, and turmoil has come.” <verse eid="JOB 3:26"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 3"/>

<chapter number="4" style="c" sid="JOB 4"/>

<para style="s">Eliphaz: The Innocent Prosper</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 4:1"/>And Eliphaz the Temanite answered and said: <verse eid="JOB 4:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 4:2"/>“Should one try a word with you, will you be wearied? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:2">And who is able to be restrained from a word? <verse eid="JOB 4:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 4:3"/>Behold, you have instructed many, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:3">and you have strengthened hands <char style="add">that are</char> weak. <verse eid="JOB 4:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 4:4"/>The one stumbling, your words, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:4">and bent knees you have strengthened. <verse eid="JOB 4:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 4:5"/>But now it has come to you, and you are weary; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:5">it touches unto you, and you are disturbed. <verse eid="JOB 4:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 4:6"/>Is not your fear your confidence, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:6">and the integrity of your ways your hope? <verse eid="JOB 4:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 4:7"/>Remember please: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 4:7">Who <char style="add">is</char> he <char style="add">who has</char> perished being innocent? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:7">And where have the upright been cut off? <verse eid="JOB 4:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 4:8"/>According to what I have seen, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:8">those plowing iniquity and sowing trouble—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:8">they shall reap it. <verse eid="JOB 4:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 4:9"/>By the breath of God they perish, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:9">and by the blast of his nose they are consumed. <verse eid="JOB 4:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 4:10"/>The roar of the lion and the voice of the fierce lion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:10">and the teeth of the young lions are broken. <verse eid="JOB 4:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 4:11"/>The lion perishes for lack of prey, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:11">and the cubs of the lioness are scattered. <verse eid="JOB 4:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 4:12"/>And to me a word was confided; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:12">and my ear took <char style="add">in</char> a whisper of it. <verse eid="JOB 4:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 4:13"/>In disquieting thoughts from visions of the night, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:13">in the falling of deep sleep upon men, <verse eid="JOB 4:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 4:14"/>dread and trembling met me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:14">and the multitude of my bones it frightened. <verse eid="JOB 4:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 4:15"/>And a spirit<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a wind</char></note> was gliding over my face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:15">the hair of my flesh bristled. <verse eid="JOB 4:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 4:16"/>It stood still, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:16">I could not discern its appearance. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 4:16">A likeness <char style="add">was</char> in front of my eyes; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:16"><char style="add">there was</char> silence, and I heard a voice: <verse eid="JOB 4:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 4:17"/>‘Shall a human be righteous more than God? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:17">Can a man be pure more than his Maker? <verse eid="JOB 4:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 4:18"/>Behold, in His servants He does not trust, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:18">and His angels He charges with error; <verse eid="JOB 4:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 4:19"/>how much more those dwelling <char style="add">in</char> houses of clay, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:19">for whom their foundation is in the dust, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:19"><char style="add">who</char> are crushed before a moth? <verse eid="JOB 4:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 4:20"/>From morning to evening they are broken to pieces; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:20">without anyone noticing, they perish forever. <verse eid="JOB 4:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 4:21"/>Has not their tent cord been pulled up with them? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 4:21">They will die, and not in wisdom?’ <verse eid="JOB 4:21"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 4"/>

<chapter number="5" style="c" sid="JOB 5"/>

<para style="s">Eliphaz Continues: God Blesses those Who Seek Him</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 5:1"/><char style="add">“</char> Call out, please. Is there one answering you? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:1">And to which of the holy ones will you turn? <verse eid="JOB 5:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 5:2"/>For indignation kills the foolish, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:2">and jealousy kills the simple. <verse eid="JOB 5:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 5:3"/>I have seen a fool taking root, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:3">and suddenly I cursed his abode. <verse eid="JOB 5:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 5:4"/>His sons are far from safety; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:4">indeed they are crushed in the gate, and <char style="add">there is</char> none rescuing; <verse eid="JOB 5:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 5:5"/>whose harvest the hungry one devours, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:5">even from among the thorns he takes it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:5">and the thirsty one pants <char style="add">after</char> their wealth.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and a snare snatches his wealth</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 5:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 5:6"/>For trouble does not come forth from the dust, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:6">nor does toil spring <char style="add">up</char> from the ground. <verse eid="JOB 5:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 5:7"/>For man is born into toil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:7">and as the sons of the flame soar to fly. <verse eid="JOB 5:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 5:8"/>But <char style="add">as for</char> me, I would seek for God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:8">and unto God I would commit my cause— <verse eid="JOB 5:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 5:9"/>the One doing great things, and there is no searching out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:9">wonders until there is no numbering. <verse eid="JOB 5:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 5:10"/>The One giving rain upon the face of the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:10">and sending waters upon the face of the outside, <verse eid="JOB 5:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 5:11"/>to set the lowly ones on high, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:11">and those mourning are high in safety. <verse eid="JOB 5:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 5:12"/><char style="add">He</char> is breaking the plots of the crafty, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:12">and their hands cannot execute wisdom. <verse eid="JOB 5:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 5:13"/>He is catching the wise in their craftiness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:13">and the counsel of those being deceptive is hurried. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in 1 Corinthians 3:19</char></note><verse eid="JOB 5:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 5:14"/>By day they encounter darkness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:14">and they grope about at midday as <char style="add">at</char> night. <verse eid="JOB 5:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 5:15"/>And He saves the needy from the sword in their mouth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:15">and from the hand of the mighty. <verse eid="JOB 5:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 5:16"/>And there is hope for the poor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:16">and injustice shuts its mouth. <verse eid="JOB 5:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 5:17"/>Behold, blessed <char style="add">is</char> the man <char style="add">whom</char> God reproves, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:17">and the discipline of Shaddai<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; here and throughout Job</char></note> you should not despise. <verse eid="JOB 5:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 5:18"/>For He brings pain, and binds up; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:18">he wounds, and his hands heal. <verse eid="JOB 5:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 5:19"/>In six distresses he will rescue you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:19">and in seven, evil shall not touch you. <verse eid="JOB 5:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 5:20"/>In famine he will redeem you from death, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:20">and in war from the hands of the sword. <verse eid="JOB 5:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 5:21"/>From the scourge of the tongue you will be hidden, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:21">and you shall not be afraid of destruction when it comes. <verse eid="JOB 5:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 5:22"/>At destruction and famine you will laugh, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:22">and of the beasts of the earth you shall not be afraid. <verse eid="JOB 5:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 5:23"/>For your covenant <char style="add">will be</char> with the stones of the field, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:23">and the beasts of the field will be at peace with you. <verse eid="JOB 5:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 5:24"/>And you will know that your tent <char style="add">is at</char> peace, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:24">and you shall visit your abode and not miss. <verse eid="JOB 5:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 5:25"/>And you will know that your seed <char style="add">is</char> numerous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:25">and your offspring like the grass of the earth. <verse eid="JOB 5:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 5:26"/>You shall come in strength to the grave, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:26">like the lifting of a sheaf in its time. <verse eid="JOB 5:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 5:27"/>Behold this—we have searched it out, <char style="add">and</char> it <char style="add">is</char> so; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 5:27">hear it, and you shall know <char style="add">it</char> for yourself.” <verse eid="JOB 5:27"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 5"/>

<chapter number="6" style="c" sid="JOB 6"/>

<para style="s">Job Replies: My Complaint Is Just</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 6:1"/>And Job answered and said: <verse eid="JOB 6:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 6:2"/>“If only my grief and my calamity could be weighed thoroughly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:2">lifting <char style="add">it</char> up together in the scales! <verse eid="JOB 6:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 6:3"/>For now it is heavy, more than the sand of the sea; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:3"><char style="add">and</char> upon thus my words have been rash. <verse eid="JOB 6:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 6:4"/>For the arrows of Shaddai<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 14</char></note> <char style="add">are</char> within me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:4">whose poison my spirit is drinking <char style="add">in</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:4">the terrors of God are arrayed against me. <verse eid="JOB 6:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 6:5"/>Does the wild donkey bray over <char style="add">its</char> grass? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:5">Or the ox bellow over its fodder? <verse eid="JOB 6:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 6:6"/>Is the unsavory eaten without salt? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:6">Or is there flavor in the white of an egg?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the sap of the mallow plant</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 6:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 6:7"/>My soul refuses to touch <char style="add">them</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:7">they <char style="add">are</char> are like disease in my food. <verse eid="JOB 6:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 6:8"/>Who shall grant <char style="add">that</char> my request would come? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:8">That God may grant my hope! <verse eid="JOB 6:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 6:9"/><char style="add">If</char> God were willing to crush me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:9">to let loose His hand and cut me off! <verse eid="JOB 6:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 6:10"/>And yet <char style="add">this</char> would be my comfort, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:10">and I would leap for joy in <char style="add">my</char> anguish—he does not spare, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 6:10">for I have not concealed </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:10">the words of the Holy One. <verse eid="JOB 6:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 6:11"/>What <char style="add">is</char> my strength, that I should hope? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:11">And what <char style="add">is</char> my end, that I should prolong my life? <verse eid="JOB 6:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 6:12"/>Is my strength the strength of stones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:12">or is my flesh <char style="add">made of</char> bronze? <verse eid="JOB 6:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 6:13"/><char style="add">Is</char> there no help for me in me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:13">when success has been taken away from me? <verse eid="JOB 6:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 6:14"/>To one despairing from his friends <char style="add">there should be</char> kindness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:14">and the fear of Shaddai he forsakes. <verse eid="JOB 6:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 6:15"/>My brothers are treacherous like a wadi, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:15">like a channel of wadis they pass away, <verse eid="JOB 6:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 6:16"/>those being darkened from the ice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:16">upon which the snow hides itself. <verse eid="JOB 6:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 6:17"/>In the time of burning <char style="add">heat</char> they are cut off; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:17">in the heat they are extinguished from their place. <verse eid="JOB 6:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 6:18"/>The caravans turn aside <char style="add">from</char> their paths; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:18">they go up into the wasteland and perish. <verse eid="JOB 6:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 6:19"/>The caravans of Tema look on; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:19">the travelers of Sheba hope for them. <verse eid="JOB 6:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 6:20"/>They are ashamed that they had trusted; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:20">they come unto her and are confounded. <verse eid="JOB 6:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 6:21"/>For now you⁺ are nothing; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:21">you⁺ see terror, and you⁺ are afraid. <verse eid="JOB 6:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 6:22"/>Is it that I said, ‘Give to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:22">or from your⁺ strength offer a bribe on my behalf? <verse eid="JOB 6:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 6:23"/>Or Deliver me from the hand of the enemy, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:23">or ransom me from the hand of dreadful ones’? <verse eid="JOB 6:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 6:24"/>teach me, and I will be silent, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:24">and give understanding to me of how I have erred. <verse eid="JOB 6:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 6:25"/>How painful are upright words! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:25">Yet what does your⁺ argument prove? <verse eid="JOB 6:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 6:26"/>Do you⁺ think to correct my words? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:26">And <char style="add">are</char> the sayings of one despairing for wind? <verse eid="JOB 6:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 6:27"/>Indeed, over the fatherless you⁺ make it fall, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:27">and you⁺ would trade away your⁺ friend. <verse eid="JOB 6:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 6:28"/>And now, may you be willing to turn toward me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:28">or would I lie to your⁺ face? <verse eid="JOB 6:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JOB 6:29"/>Turn, please, let there not be injustice; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:29">and turn even now—my righteousness <char style="add">is</char> in it. <verse eid="JOB 6:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JOB 6:30"/>Is there injustice on my tongue? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 6:30">Can my palate not discern malice? <verse eid="JOB 6:30"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 6"/>

<chapter number="7" style="c" sid="JOB 7"/>

<para style="s">Job Continues: Life Seems Futile</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 7:1"/><char style="add">“</char> Is there not hard service for man on earth? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:1">Are his days like the days of a hireling? <verse eid="JOB 7:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 7:2"/>As a servant longs for shade, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:2">and as a hireling awaits his wages, <verse eid="JOB 7:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 7:3"/>so are allotted to me months of emptiness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:3">and nights of toil are appointed to me. <verse eid="JOB 7:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 7:4"/>When I lie down, then I say, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:4">‘When shall I arise?’ </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 7:4">But the night is measured out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:4">and I am full of tossings until dawn. <verse eid="JOB 7:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 7:5"/>My flesh is clothed <char style="add">with</char> worm and clod of the dust; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:5">my skin breaks and festers. <verse eid="JOB 7:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 7:6"/>My days are swifter than a weaver’s shuttle; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:6">and they end without hope. <verse eid="JOB 7:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 7:7"/>Remember that my life is a breath; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:7">my eye shall not return to see good. <verse eid="JOB 7:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 7:8"/>The eye of the one seeing me shall not behold me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:8">your eyes <char style="add">are</char> on me, and I will be no more. <verse eid="JOB 7:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 7:9"/>As a cloud is consumed and goes away, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:9">so the one going down <char style="add">to</char> Sheol does not ascend. <verse eid="JOB 7:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 7:10"/>He shall not return again to his house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:10">nor shall his place recognize him anymore. <verse eid="JOB 7:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 7:11"/>So I will not restrain my mouth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:11">I will speak in the distress of my spirit; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:11">I will complain in the bitterness of my soul. <verse eid="JOB 7:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 7:12"/><char style="add">Am</char> I a sea or the sea monster, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:12">that You would set a guard over me? <verse eid="JOB 7:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 7:13"/>When I say, My bed will comfort me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:13">my couch will lift my complaint, <verse eid="JOB 7:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 7:14"/>then You shatter me with dreams </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:14">and terrify me with visions, <verse eid="JOB 7:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 7:15"/>so that my soul would choose strangling <char style="add">and</char> death </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:15">rather than my bones. <verse eid="JOB 7:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 7:16"/>I loathe—I would not live forever! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:16">Cease from me, for my days are vapor. <verse eid="JOB 7:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 7:17"/>What <char style="add">is</char> man that You should magnify him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:17">and that You would set Your heart toward him, <verse eid="JOB 7:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 7:18"/>that You attend to him in the mornings; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:18">in the moments You will test him? <verse eid="JOB 7:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 7:19"/>How long will You not look away from me? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:19">Will You not leave me alone until I swallow my spittle? <verse eid="JOB 7:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 7:20"/><char style="add">If</char> I have sinned, what have I done to You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:20">O watcher of mankind? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 7:20">Why have You set me to <char style="add">be</char> a target for You </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:20">and <char style="add">why</char> should I be a burden to <char style="add">You</char>?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to myself</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 7:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 7:21"/>And why do You not lift my transgression </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:21">and make my iniquity pass away? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 7:21">For now in the dust I shall lie down, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 7:21">and You will seek me, and I <char style="add">will</char> not be there.” <verse eid="JOB 7:21"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 7"/>

<chapter number="8" style="c" sid="JOB 8"/>

<para style="s">Bildad: Job Should Repent</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 8:1"/>And Bildad the Shuhite answered and said: <verse eid="JOB 8:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 8:2"/>“Until when will you speak these <char style="add">things</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:2">and the words of your mouth <char style="add">be</char> a mighty wind? <verse eid="JOB 8:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 8:3"/>Does God pervert judgment? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:3">Or <char style="add">does</char> Shaddai pervert justice? <verse eid="JOB 8:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 8:4"/>If your sons have sinned against Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:4">then He has sent them into the hand of their transgression. <verse eid="JOB 8:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 8:5"/>If you seek diligently for God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:5">and ask Shaddai for favor, <verse eid="JOB 8:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 8:6"/>if you <char style="add">are</char> pure and upright, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:6">surely now He will rouse Himself over you </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:6">and restore the abode of your righteousness. <verse eid="JOB 8:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 8:7"/>And your beginning was small, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:7">and your end will greatly increase. <verse eid="JOB 8:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 8:8"/>For inquire, please, of the former generation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:8">and consider the finding of their fathers. <verse eid="JOB 8:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 8:9"/>For we <char style="add">are</char> of yesterday, and we do not know; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:9">indeed, our days <char style="add">are</char> a shadow upon the earth. <verse eid="JOB 8:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 8:10"/>Will they not instruct you and speak to you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:10">and from their heart bring forth words? <verse eid="JOB 8:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 8:11"/>Can the papyrus rise up without a marsh? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:11">Can the reed grow without waters? <verse eid="JOB 8:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 8:12"/>It is still in its greenness—it is not cut down, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:12">and before all grass, it withers. <verse eid="JOB 8:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 8:13"/>So <char style="add">are</char> the paths of all those forgetting God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:13">and the hope of the godless will perish, <verse eid="JOB 8:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 8:14"/>for whom his confidence shall be cut off, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:14">and his trust the house of a spider. <verse eid="JOB 8:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 8:15"/>He leans upon his house, and it does not stand; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:15">he takes firm hold on it, and it does not arise. <verse eid="JOB 8:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 8:16"/>He <char style="add">is</char> lush before the face of the sun, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:16">and over his garden, his shoot goes forth; <verse eid="JOB 8:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 8:17"/>over a rock-pile his roots are wrapped, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:17">he looks for a house of stones. <verse eid="JOB 8:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 8:18"/>If one destroys him from his place, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:18">then it will disown him: ‘I have not seen you.’ <verse eid="JOB 8:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 8:19"/>Behold, this is the joy of his way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:19">and from the dust another sprouts up. <verse eid="JOB 8:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 8:20"/>Behold, God will not reject the blameless, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:20">and He will not strengthen the hand of those doing evil. <verse eid="JOB 8:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 8:21"/>Yet He will fill your mouth <char style="add">with</char> laughter, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:21">and your lips with a shout of joy. <verse eid="JOB 8:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 8:22"/>Those hating you will be clothed <char style="add">with</char> shame, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 8:22">and the tent of the wicked <char style="add">will be</char> no more.” </para>

<para style="p" vid="JOB 8:22"> <char style="add">Shaddai</char> means <char style="add">the Almighty</char>; also in verse 5<verse eid="JOB 8:22"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 8"/>

<chapter number="9" style="c" sid="JOB 9"/>

<para style="s">Job: How Can I Contend with God?</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 9:1"/>And Job answered and said, <verse eid="JOB 9:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 9:2"/>“Truly I know that <char style="add">it is</char> so. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:2">But how can a man be righteous with God? <verse eid="JOB 9:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 9:3"/>If one was delighted to contend with Him,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">If He wished to contend with someone</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:3">he could not answer Him one <char style="add">time</char> out of a thousand. <verse eid="JOB 9:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 9:4"/><char style="add">He is</char> wise of heart and firm of strength; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:4">who has hardened <char style="add">himself</char> against Him and been whole? <verse eid="JOB 9:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 9:5"/>He moves the mountains, and they do not know when </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:5">He overturns them in His anger. <verse eid="JOB 9:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 9:6"/>He shakes the earth from its place, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:6">and its pillars shudder. <verse eid="JOB 9:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 9:7"/>He speaks to the sun, and it does not rise,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">shine</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:7">and He seals up the stars, <verse eid="JOB 9:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 9:8"/>stretching out the heavens by himself, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:8">and treading upon the heights of the sea. <verse eid="JOB 9:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 9:9"/>Making the Bear <char style="add">and</char> Orion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:9">and the Pleiades and the chambers of the south, <verse eid="JOB 9:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 9:10"/>doing great <char style="add">things</char> until there is no searching out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:10">and wonders until there is no numbering. <verse eid="JOB 9:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 9:11"/>Behold, He passes by over me, and I do not see <char style="add">Him</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:11">and He moves past, and I do not perceive Him. <verse eid="JOB 9:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 9:12"/>Behold, He snatches away,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">snatches someone in death</char></note> <char style="add">and</char> who will turn Him back? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:12">Who shall say to Him, ‘What are You doing?’ <verse eid="JOB 9:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 9:13"/>God will not turn aside His nose—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:13">beneath Him bowed the helpers of Rahab! <verse eid="JOB 9:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 9:14"/>How then can I answer Him </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:14"><char style="add">and</char> choose my words with Him, <verse eid="JOB 9:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 9:15"/>whom, if I were righteous, I could not answer; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:15">to my Judge I would plead for mercy. <verse eid="JOB 9:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 9:16"/>If I called and He answered me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:16">I could not believe that He gives ear <char style="add">to</char> my voice— <verse eid="JOB 9:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 9:17"/><char style="add">He</char> who crushes me with a tempest, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:17">and multiplies my wounds without cause. <verse eid="JOB 9:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 9:18"/>He does not allow me to return my breath, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:18">but He fills me <char style="add">with</char> bitterness. <verse eid="JOB 9:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 9:19"/>If <char style="add">it is</char> of power, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:19">behold, <char style="add">He is</char> mighty; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 9:19">and if of justice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:19">who can summon <char style="add">Him</char>?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See LXX; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">summon me</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 9:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 9:20"/>If I were righteous, my own mouth would declare me wicked; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:20">if I were blameless, then it would declare me perverse.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He would declare me guilty</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 9:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 9:21"/>I <char style="add">am</char> blameless; I do not know my soul; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:21">I despise my life. <verse eid="JOB 9:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 9:22"/>It <char style="add">is</char> one <char style="add">thing</char>! <char style="add">And</char> upon thus I say, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:22">‘The blameless and the wicked He brings to an end.’ <verse eid="JOB 9:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 9:23"/>If the whip kills suddenly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:23">He mocks the despair of the innocent. <verse eid="JOB 9:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 9:24"/>The earth is given into the hand of the wicked; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:24">He covers the faces of its judges—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:24">If not, then who is it? <verse eid="JOB 9:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 9:25"/>So my days are swifter than a runner; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:25">they flee, not seeing good. <verse eid="JOB 9:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 9:26"/>They pass by with ships of papyrus, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:26">like an eagle rushing upon its food. <verse eid="JOB 9:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 9:27"/>If I were to say, ‘I will forget my complaint, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:27">let me change my face and smile,’ <verse eid="JOB 9:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 9:28"/>I would fear all my sorrows, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:28"><char style="add">and</char> I know that You will not clear me. <verse eid="JOB 9:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JOB 9:29"/>I am wicked; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:29">why then should I labor in vain? <verse eid="JOB 9:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JOB 9:30"/>If I wash myself with water of snow,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">soap</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:30">and cleanse my hands with lye, <verse eid="JOB 9:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JOB 9:31"/>yet into the pit You will plunge me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:31">and my own garments will abhor me. <verse eid="JOB 9:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="JOB 9:32"/>For <char style="add">He is</char> not a man like I <char style="add">am</char>, <char style="add">that</char> I may answer Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:32">that we would come together into judgment. <verse eid="JOB 9:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="JOB 9:33"/>There is not a mediator between us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:33">to lay his hand upon the two of us, <verse eid="JOB 9:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="JOB 9:34"/>tu turn away from me His rod, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:34">and not let His terror frighten me. <verse eid="JOB 9:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="JOB 9:35"/>I would speak and not be afraid of Him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 9:35">but I <char style="add">am</char> not thus with me. <verse eid="JOB 9:35"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 9"/>

<chapter number="10" style="c" sid="JOB 10"/>

<para style="s">Job’s Plea to God</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 10:1"/><char style="add">“</char> My soul Is weary of my life; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:1">I will leave upon myself my complaint; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:1">I will speak in the bitterness of my soul. <verse eid="JOB 10:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 10:2"/>I will say to God: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:2">Do not condemn me! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:2">Let me know over what You contend with me. <verse eid="JOB 10:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 10:3"/>Is it good to You that You oppress, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:3">that You despise the work of Your hands, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:3">and upon the counsel of the wicked You shine? <verse eid="JOB 10:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 10:4"/>Are eyes of flesh unto You? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:4">Or do You see according to the seeing of a man? <verse eid="JOB 10:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 10:5"/>Are Your days like the days of a man? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:5">Or <char style="add">are</char> Your years like the days of a man, <verse eid="JOB 10:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 10:6"/>that You would seek for my iniquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:6">and would search for my sin— <verse eid="JOB 10:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 10:7"/>upon Your knowledge that I am not wicked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:7">and there is no delivering from Your hand? <verse eid="JOB 10:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 10:8"/>Your hands formed me and made me entirely round about, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:8">yet You swallowed me up! <verse eid="JOB 10:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 10:9"/>Remember, please, that You made me as <char style="add">from</char> the clay. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:9">And will You return me to the dust? <verse eid="JOB 10:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 10:10"/>Was <char style="add">it</char> not like milk <char style="add">that</char> You poured me out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:10">and like cheese You curdled me? <verse eid="JOB 10:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 10:11"/><char style="add">With</char> skin and flesh You clothed me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:11">and with bones and sinews You knit me together. <verse eid="JOB 10:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 10:12"/>Life and loving devotion<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Forms of the Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">chesed</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as </char><char style="fq" closed="false">loving devotion</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; the range of meaning includes </char><char style="fq" closed="false">love</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">goodness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">kindness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">faithfulness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, and </char><char style="fq" closed="false">mercy</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, as well as </char><char style="fq" closed="false">loyalty to a covenant</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> You have done with me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:12">and Your care has guarded my spirit. <verse eid="JOB 10:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 10:13"/>And these You have hidden in Your heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:13">I know that this was with You. <verse eid="JOB 10:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 10:14"/>If I sin then You keep watch on me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:14">and You will not clear me from my iniquity. <verse eid="JOB 10:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 10:15"/>If I am wicked, woe to me! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:15">And <char style="add">if</char> I am righteous, I cannot lift up my head; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 10:15"><char style="add">I am</char> full of shame, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:15">and seeing my affliction. <verse eid="JOB 10:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 10:16"/>And should it arise—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:16">as a lion You would hunt me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:16">and turn back <char style="add">and</char> work wonders against me. <verse eid="JOB 10:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 10:17"/>You renew Your witnesses against me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:17">and increase Your indignation with me; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 10:17">changes and warfare </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:17">are with me. <verse eid="JOB 10:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 10:18"/>And why did You bring me forth from the womb? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:18">Would that I had expired, and an eye had not seen me, <verse eid="JOB 10:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 10:19"/>as though I had never come to be—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:19">that I came from the womb <char style="add">and</char> was carried to the grave! <verse eid="JOB 10:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 10:20"/>Are not my days few? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:20">Then cease and withdraw from me, and let me smile a little, <verse eid="JOB 10:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 10:21"/>before I go—and I shall not return—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:21">to the land of darkness and the shadow of death, <verse eid="JOB 10:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 10:22"/>a land of obscurity like thick darkness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:22">of the shadow of death, and no order, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 10:22">and it shines like deep darkness.” <verse eid="JOB 10:22"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 10"/>

<chapter number="11" style="c" sid="JOB 11"/>

<para style="s">Zophar Rebukes Job</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 11:1"/>Then Zophar the Naamathite answered, and said: <verse eid="JOB 11:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 11:2"/>“Shall a multitude of words not be answered? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:2">And should a man of lips be justified? <verse eid="JOB 11:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 11:3"/>Shall your idle boasts cause men to be silent? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:3">And will you mock, and no one is ashamed? <verse eid="JOB 11:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 11:4"/>For you have said, ‘My doctrine <char style="add">is</char> pure, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:4">and I am clean in Your eyes.’ <verse eid="JOB 11:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 11:5"/>But who will give God to speak, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:5">and open His lips against you, <verse eid="JOB 11:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 11:6"/>and declare to you the secrets of wisdom—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:6">for <char style="add">there are</char> two sides to wisdom. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 11:6">And know that God forgets </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:6">some of your iniquity. <verse eid="JOB 11:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 11:7"/>Can you find out the searching of God? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:7">Or can you find out unto the limit of Shaddai?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 11:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 11:8"/>The heights of the heavens—what can you do? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:8"><char style="add">They are</char> deeper than Sheol—what can you know? <verse eid="JOB 11:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 11:9"/>Longer than the earth <char style="add">is</char> its measure, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:9">and wider than the sea. <verse eid="JOB 11:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 11:10"/>If He passes by and imprisons and assembles, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:10">then who can turn Him back? <verse eid="JOB 11:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 11:11"/>For He knows the men of vanity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:11">and He sees iniquity—<char style="add">will</char> He not then discern <char style="add">it</char>? <verse eid="JOB 11:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 11:12"/>But a man <char style="add">who is</char> hollow will become wise </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:12">when the colt of a wild donkey is born <char style="add">as</char> a man!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">is born tame</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 11:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 11:13"/>If you would prepare your heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:13">and stretch out your hands to Him, <verse eid="JOB 11:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 11:14"/>if iniquity is in your hand, put it far away, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:14">and do not let injustice dwell in your tents. <verse eid="JOB 11:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 11:15"/>Surely then you could lift up your face without blemish, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:15">and you could be established and not fear. <verse eid="JOB 11:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 11:16"/>For you would forget <char style="add">your</char> toil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:16"><char style="add">and</char> remember <char style="add">it</char> as waters pass by. <verse eid="JOB 11:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 11:17"/>And more than noon life will arise; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:17">darkness will become like the morning. <verse eid="JOB 11:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 11:18"/>And you will be secure, because there is hope, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:18">and you will search <char style="add">and</char> lie down in safety. <verse eid="JOB 11:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 11:19"/>Then You will lie down, and there will be no one making <char style="add">you</char> tremble, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:19">and many will seek favor <char style="add">from</char> your face. <verse eid="JOB 11:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 11:20"/>But the eyes of the wicked will fail, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:20">and escape will perish from them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 11:20">and their hope <char style="add">be</char> a puff of the soul.” <verse eid="JOB 11:20"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 11"/>

<chapter number="12" style="c" sid="JOB 12"/>

<para style="s">Job Presents His Case</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 12:1"/>And Job answered and said, <verse eid="JOB 12:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 12:2"/>“Truly <char style="add">it is</char> that you⁺ <char style="add">are</char> the people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:2">and wisdom will die with you⁺. <verse eid="JOB 12:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 12:3"/>Also unto me <char style="add">is</char> a heart like you⁺; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:3">I <char style="add">am</char> not falling below you⁺. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:3">And with whom are not <char style="add">things</char> like these? <verse eid="JOB 12:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 12:4"/>I have become a laughingstock to his neighbor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:4">one calling on God and He answered him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:4">righteous <char style="add">and</char> blameless—a laughingstock. <verse eid="JOB 12:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 12:5"/><char style="add">There is</char> contempt for disaster in the thought of the secure, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:5">prepared for those slipping of foot. <verse eid="JOB 12:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 12:6"/>The tents of robbers are at rest, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:6">and those disturbing God are secure—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:6">to the one who carries <char style="add">his</char> god in his hand.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">though God keeps them in His hand</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 12:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 12:7"/>But ask now the beasts, and they will instruct you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:7">and the birds of the heavens, and one will declare to you. <verse eid="JOB 12:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 12:8"/>Or speak to the earth and it will instruct you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:8">and the fish of the sea and they will recount to you. <verse eid="JOB 12:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 12:9"/>Who among all these does not know </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:9">that the hand of YHWH has done this— <verse eid="JOB 12:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 12:10"/>in whose hand <char style="add">is</char> the soul of every living <char style="add">thing</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:10">and the breath of all the flesh of man? <verse eid="JOB 12:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 12:11"/>Does not the ear examine words, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:11">and the mouth taste food for itself? <verse eid="JOB 12:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 12:12"/>With the aged is wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:12">and in length of days is understanding. <verse eid="JOB 12:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 12:13"/>With Him <char style="add">are</char> wisdom and strength; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:13">unto Him <char style="add">are</char> counsel and understanding. <verse eid="JOB 12:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 12:14"/>Behold, He tears down, and it cannot be rebuilt; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:14">He closes <char style="add">up</char> upon a man, and it cannot be opened. <verse eid="JOB 12:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 12:15"/>Behold, He restrains the waters and they dry up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:15">and He sends them forth and they overthrow the land. <verse eid="JOB 12:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 12:16"/>With Him <char style="add">are</char> strength and wisdom </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:16">and unto Him <char style="add">are</char> the deceived and the deceiver. <verse eid="JOB 12:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 12:17"/>He leads away counselors barefoot, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:17">and judges He makes foolish. <verse eid="JOB 12:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 12:18"/>The bond of kings He loosens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:18">and He binds a waistband around their loins. <verse eid="JOB 12:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 12:19"/>He leads away priests barefoot, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:19">and the established He overthrows. <verse eid="JOB 12:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 12:20"/>He deprives the lip of the trusted ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:20">and the discernment of the elders He takes away. <verse eid="JOB 12:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 12:21"/>He pours out contempt on nobles, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:21">and the mighty He makes feeble. <verse eid="JOB 12:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 12:22"/>He uncovers deep things out of darkness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:22">and brings to light the shadow of death. <verse eid="JOB 12:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 12:23"/>He makes great nations, and destroys them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:23">He enlarges nations and guides them away. <verse eid="JOB 12:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 12:24"/>He turns aside the understanding of the chiefs of the people of the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:24">and makes them wander in a wilderness without a path. <verse eid="JOB 12:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 12:25"/>They feel <char style="add">about</char> <char style="add">in</char> darkness without light, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 12:25">and He makes them stagger like a drunkard. <verse eid="JOB 12:25"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 12"/>

<chapter number="13" style="c" sid="JOB 13"/>

<para style="s">Job Prepares His Case</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 13:1"/><char style="add">“</char> Behold, all <char style="add">this</char> my eye has seen; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:1">my ear has heard and understood it. <verse eid="JOB 13:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 13:2"/>According to your⁺ knowledge, I also know; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:2">I am not falling below you⁺. <verse eid="JOB 13:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 13:3"/>But I wish to speak to Shaddai,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:3">and to reason with God I desire. <verse eid="JOB 13:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 13:4"/>But you⁺, are plasterers of a lie, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:4">worthless physicians all of you⁺. <verse eid="JOB 13:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 13:5"/>Who will give <char style="add">that</char> you will surely remain silent, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:5">and it will be for wisdom for you⁺. <verse eid="JOB 13:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 13:6"/>Hear now my reasoning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:6">and be attentive to the quarreling of my lips. <verse eid="JOB 13:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 13:7"/>Will you⁺ speak injustice for God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:7">and will you⁺ speak deceit for Him? <verse eid="JOB 13:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 13:8"/>Will you⁺ lift His face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:8">or will you⁺ contend for God? <verse eid="JOB 13:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 13:9"/>Will <char style="add">it be</char> good when He searches you⁺ out? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:9">Or as one mocks a man, can you⁺ mock Him? <verse eid="JOB 13:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 13:10"/>He will surely rebuke you⁺, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:10">if in secrecy you⁺ were lifting faces. <verse eid="JOB 13:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 13:11"/>Will not His excellence terrify you⁺ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:11">and the dread of Him fall upon you⁺? <verse eid="JOB 13:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 13:12"/>Your⁺ remembrances <char style="add">are</char> proverbs of ashes; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:12">your⁺ defenses <char style="add">are</char> defenses of clay. <verse eid="JOB 13:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 13:13"/>Keep silent from me, and I will speak, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:13">and let come upon me what may. <verse eid="JOB 13:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 13:14"/>For what do I take up my flesh in my teeth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:14">and my soul do I set in my palm? <verse eid="JOB 13:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 13:15"/>Behold, He may slay me; unto Him I will hope.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I have no other hope</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:15">Indeed, my ways to His face I will defend. <verse eid="JOB 13:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 13:16"/>Even this <char style="add">may be</char> unto me salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:16">for the godless one shall not come <char style="add">in</char> before His face. <verse eid="JOB 13:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 13:17"/>Listen <char style="add">with</char> hearing <char style="add">to</char> my speech, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:17">and may my declaration <char style="add">be</char> in your⁺ ears. <verse eid="JOB 13:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 13:18"/>Behold, now, I have arranged my defense. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:18">I know that I am righteous. <verse eid="JOB 13:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 13:19"/>Who <char style="add">is</char> he <char style="add">who</char> will contend with me? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:19">For then I would be silent and die. <verse eid="JOB 13:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 13:20"/>Only two <char style="add">things</char> may You not do with me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:20">then from Your face I will not hide myself. <verse eid="JOB 13:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 13:21"/>Withdraw your hand from me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:21">and do not let Your terror terrify me. <verse eid="JOB 13:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 13:22"/>And call, and I will answer; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:22">or let me speak, and You reply. <verse eid="JOB 13:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 13:23"/>How many <char style="add">are</char> the iniquities and sins for me? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:23">Make me know my transgression and my sin. <verse eid="JOB 13:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 13:24"/>Why do You hide Your face </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:24">and consider me as an enemy unto You? <verse eid="JOB 13:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 13:25"/>Would You make tremble a leaf driven away, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:25">and would You pursue dry stubble? <verse eid="JOB 13:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 13:26"/>For You write against me bitter <char style="add">things</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:26">and you make me inherit the iniquities of my youth. <verse eid="JOB 13:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 13:27"/>And You put my feet in the stock, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:27">and You watch all my paths; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 13:27">upon the soles of my feet </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:27">You engrave. <verse eid="JOB 13:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 13:28"/>And he, like a rotten thing, is worn out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 13:28">like a garment a moth has eaten. <verse eid="JOB 13:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 13"/>

<chapter number="14" style="c" sid="JOB 14"/>

<para style="s">Job Laments the Finality of Death</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 14:1"/><char style="add">“</char> Man, born of a woman, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:1"><char style="add">is</char> short of days and full of trouble. <verse eid="JOB 14:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 14:2"/>Like a flower he comes forth and withers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:2">and he flees like a shadow, and does not stand. <verse eid="JOB 14:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 14:3"/>And upon this one do You open Your eyes; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:3">and bring me into judgment with You? <verse eid="JOB 14:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 14:4"/>Who will bring clean from unclean? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:4">Not one! <verse eid="JOB 14:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 14:5"/>Since his days are determined, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:5">the number of his months <char style="add">is</char> with You; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 14:5">his limits You have made, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:5">and he cannot pass over <char style="add">them</char>. <verse eid="JOB 14:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 14:6"/>Look away from him that he may rest, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:6">until he can enjoy his day like a hireling. <verse eid="JOB 14:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 14:7"/>For there is hope for a tree, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:7">if it is cut down, that again it will pass through, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:7">and its tender shoots will not cease. <verse eid="JOB 14:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 14:8"/>Though its root may grow old in the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:8">and its stump may die in the dirt, <verse eid="JOB 14:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 14:9"/>from the scent of water it will sprout, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:9">and will make branch<char style="add">es</char> like a <char style="add">fresh</char> planting. <verse eid="JOB 14:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 14:10"/>And a man dies and is laid low; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:10">and a man expires, and where <char style="add">is</char> he? <verse eid="JOB 14:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 14:11"/>As waters disappear from the sea, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:11">and a river dries up and withers, <verse eid="JOB 14:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 14:12"/>so a man lies down </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:12">and does not arise; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 14:12">until the heavens <char style="add">are</char> no more, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:12">they will not awaken and they will not be roused from their sleep. <verse eid="JOB 14:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 14:13"/>Who will give <char style="add">that</char> You would hide me in Sheol, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:13"><char style="add">that</char> You would hide me until the turning back of Your anger, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 14:13"><char style="add">that</char> You would set for me a limit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:13">and then remember me! <verse eid="JOB 14:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 14:14"/>If a man dies, will he live? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:14">All the days of my hardship, I will wait, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:14">until the coming of my change.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">my renewal</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">my relief</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 14:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 14:15"/>You will call, and I will answer You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:15">You will desire the work of Your hands. <verse eid="JOB 14:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 14:16"/>For now, You count my steps; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:16">You do not watch over my sin. <verse eid="JOB 14:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 14:17"/>My transgression is sealed up in a bundle, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:17">and You plaster over my iniquity. <verse eid="JOB 14:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 14:18"/>But <char style="add">as</char> a falling mountain wastes away, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:18">and <char style="add">as</char> a rock moves from its place, <verse eid="JOB 14:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 14:19"/><char style="add">as</char> stones <char style="add">by</char> the waters are worn away, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:19"><char style="add">and</char> her torrents engulf the dust of the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:19">so the hope of man You destroy. <verse eid="JOB 14:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 14:20"/>You prevail over him forever, and he goes away; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:20">You change his face and send him away. <verse eid="JOB 14:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 14:21"/>His sons gain honor, and he does not know <char style="add">it</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:21">and they are diminished, and he does not perceive it. <verse eid="JOB 14:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 14:22"/>Indeed his flesh upon him is in pain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 14:22">and his soul mourns over him.” <verse eid="JOB 14:22"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 14"/>

<chapter number="15" style="c" sid="JOB 15"/>

<para style="s">Eliphaz: Job Does Not Fear God</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 15:1"/>Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered and said: <verse eid="JOB 15:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 15:2"/>“Does a wise one answer <char style="add">with</char> knowledge of wind, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:2">and fill his belly <char style="add">with</char> the east wind? <verse eid="JOB 15:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 15:3"/>Should he reason with a word that does not benefit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:3">and with words without profit in them? <verse eid="JOB 15:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 15:4"/>Indeed, you break apart fear, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:4">and diminish meditation before the face of God. <verse eid="JOB 15:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 15:5"/>For your iniquity teaches your mouth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:5">and you choose the tongue of the crafty. <verse eid="JOB 15:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 15:6"/>Your own mouth declares you wicked, and not I; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:6">and your lips testify against you. <verse eid="JOB 15:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 15:7"/>Were you born <char style="add">as</char> the first man? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:7">And were you formed before the face of the hills? <verse eid="JOB 15:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 15:8"/>Do you listen in the council of God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:8">and reduce to yourself wisdom? <verse eid="JOB 15:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 15:9"/>What do you know that we do not know? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:9"><char style="add">What</char> do you understand that <char style="add">is</char> not with us? <verse eid="JOB 15:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 15:10"/>Even the gray-haired and the aged are with us—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:10">greater than your father <char style="add">in</char> days. <verse eid="JOB 15:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 15:11"/>Are the consolations of God too small for you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:11">or a word in gentleness to you? <verse eid="JOB 15:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 15:12"/>Why does your heart carry you away, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:12">and why do your eyes flash,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">blink</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 15:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 15:13"/>that you should turn your spirit against God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:13">and bring out <char style="add">such</char> words out of your mouth? <verse eid="JOB 15:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 15:14"/>What <char style="add">is</char> man that he should be pure, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:14">or that he should be righteous, one born of woman? <verse eid="JOB 15:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 15:15"/>Behold, He does not trust in His holy ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:15">and the heavens are not pure in His eyes; <verse eid="JOB 15:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 15:16"/>also surely the abominable and corrupt one </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:16"><char style="add">is</char> a man drinking iniquity like water! <verse eid="JOB 15:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 15:17"/>I will tell you! Listen to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:17">and this <char style="add">that</char> I have seen I will recount— <verse eid="JOB 15:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 15:18"/>what the wise have brought forward </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:18">and have not concealed from their fathers, <verse eid="JOB 15:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 15:19"/>to whom alone the land was given, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:19">and a stranger did not pass over in their midst. <verse eid="JOB 15:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 15:20"/>All the days of the wicked, he is writhing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:20">and the number of years is hidden for the ruthless. <verse eid="JOB 15:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 15:21"/>The voice of dread <char style="add">is</char> in his ears; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:21">in prosperity, the destroyer comes upon him. <verse eid="JOB 15:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 15:22"/>He is not sure to return from darkness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:22">and he <char style="add">is</char> watched over unto the sword. <verse eid="JOB 15:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 15:23"/>He <char style="add">is</char> is wandering for bread for vultures, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:23">knowing that a day of darkness <char style="add">is</char> ready at his hand. <verse eid="JOB 15:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 15:24"/>Distress and anguish terrify him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:24">they prevail against him like a king ready for the attack. <verse eid="JOB 15:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 15:25"/>For he stretched out his hand against God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:25">and against Shaddai<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char></note> he sought to prevail, <verse eid="JOB 15:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 15:26"/>running against Him with the neck, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:26"><char style="add">with</char> thickness of the bosses of his shields. <verse eid="JOB 15:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 15:27"/>For he has covered his face with his fat, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:27">and made thick fat upon <char style="add">his</char> loin. <verse eid="JOB 15:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 15:28"/>And he dwells in desolate cities, houses in which they do not dwell, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:28">which are ready to be heaps. <verse eid="JOB 15:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JOB 15:29"/>He will not be rich, and his wealth will not stand, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:29">nor will <char style="add">his</char> possessions stretch out over the earth. <verse eid="JOB 15:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JOB 15:30"/>He will not turn aside from darkness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:30">the flame will dry out his shoot, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:30">and he will turn aside at the breath of His mouth. <verse eid="JOB 15:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JOB 15:31"/>Do not let him trust in emptiness, deceiving himself, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:31">for emptiness will be his recompense. <verse eid="JOB 15:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="JOB 15:32"/>Not in his day will it be fulfilled, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:32">and his branch will not be green. <verse eid="JOB 15:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="JOB 15:33"/>He will shake off his unripe grape like a vine, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:33">and he will cast off his blossom like an olive tree. <verse eid="JOB 15:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="JOB 15:34"/>For the company of the godless <char style="add">is</char> barren, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:34">and fire will consume the tents of bribery. <verse eid="JOB 15:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="JOB 15:35"/>They conceive trouble and give birth to inquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 15:35">and their belly prepares deceit.” <verse eid="JOB 15:35"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 15"/>

<chapter number="16" style="c" sid="JOB 16"/>

<para style="s">Job Decries His Comforters</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 16:1"/>And Job answered and said: <verse eid="JOB 16:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 16:2"/>“I have heard many such things, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:2">all of you⁺ comforters of trouble. <verse eid="JOB 16:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 16:3"/><char style="add">Is</char> an end to words of wind? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:3">Or what compels you that you answer? <verse eid="JOB 16:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 16:4"/>I also could speak as you⁺, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:4">if your⁺ soul were in place of my soul; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 16:4">I could join together words against you⁺, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:4">and shake at you⁺ with my head. <verse eid="JOB 16:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 16:5"/>I could strengthen you⁺ with my mouth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:5">and the moving of my lips would bring relief. <verse eid="JOB 16:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 16:6"/>If I speak, my sorrow is not relieved; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:6">and <char style="add">if</char> I cease, how will it go from me? <verse eid="JOB 16:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 16:7"/>Surely now He has worn me out; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:7">You have devastated all my company. <verse eid="JOB 16:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 16:8"/>You have bound me—it is a witness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:8">and my leanness rises up against me; it testifies against my face. <verse eid="JOB 16:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 16:9"/><char style="add">In</char> His anger He tears <char style="add">me</char> and hates me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:9">He gnashes at me with His teeth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:9">My adversary sharpens His eyes against me. <verse eid="JOB 16:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 16:10"/>They gape at me with their mouth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:10">in scorn they strike my cheeks; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:10">as one they mass themselves against me. <verse eid="JOB 16:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 16:11"/>God shuts me up to the ungodly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:11">and upon the hands of the wicked He wrings me out. <verse eid="JOB 16:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 16:12"/>I was at ease, and He broke me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:12">and He seized me by my neck and shattered me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:12">and stood me up for Him as a target. <verse eid="JOB 16:12"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 16:13"/>His archers circle round against me; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 16:13">He splits my kidneys and does not spare; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:13">He pours out my gall on the ground. <verse eid="JOB 16:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 16:14"/>He breaches me, breach upon face of the breach; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:14">He runs upon me like a warrior. <verse eid="JOB 16:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 16:15"/>I have sewn sackcloth over my skin, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:15">and I have thrust my horn into the dust. <verse eid="JOB 16:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 16:16"/>My face is red from weeping, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:16">and on my eyelids <char style="add">is</char> the shadow of death, <verse eid="JOB 16:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 16:17"/>although violence is not in my hands, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:17">and my prayer <char style="add">is</char> pure. <verse eid="JOB 16:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 16:18"/>O earth, may you not cover my blood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:18">and let there not be a place for my cry! <verse eid="JOB 16:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 16:19"/>Even now, behold! My testimony <char style="add">is</char> in the heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:19">and my witness <char style="add">is</char> in the heights. <verse eid="JOB 16:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 16:20"/>My friends are mocking me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:20">my eye pours out to God. <verse eid="JOB 16:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 16:21"/>And he reasons for a man with God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:21">and <char style="add">as</char> a son of man for his friend. <verse eid="JOB 16:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 16:22"/>For the years of <char style="add">my</char> number have come, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 16:22">and the path of no return I shall walk. <verse eid="JOB 16:22"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 16"/>

<chapter number="17" style="c" sid="JOB 17"/>

<para style="s">Job Prepares for Death</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 17:1"/><char style="add">“</char> My spirit is destroyed, my days are extinguished—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:1">graves are for me. <verse eid="JOB 17:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 17:2"/>If not, mockers <char style="add">are</char> with me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:2">and in their provocation my eye lodges. <verse eid="JOB 17:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 17:3"/>Place, please, my pledge with You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:3">who <char style="add">is</char> he who will strike himself to my hand? <verse eid="JOB 17:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 17:4"/>For You have hidden their heart from understanding, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:4"><char style="add">and</char> upon thus You will not exalt <char style="add">them</char>. <verse eid="JOB 17:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 17:5"/>He reports <char style="add">his</char> friends for a portion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:5">and the eyes of his sons are consumed. <verse eid="JOB 17:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 17:6"/>And He has made me a byword among the peoples, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:6">and a spitting in the face I have become. <verse eid="JOB 17:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 17:7"/>And my eye is dim from sorrow, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:7">and my members <char style="add">are</char> like a shadow, all of them. <verse eid="JOB 17:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 17:8"/>The upright are appalled at this, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:8">and the innocent rouses himself against the godless. <verse eid="JOB 17:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 17:9"/>Yet the righteous shall hold to his way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:9">and the one clean of hands shall add strength. <verse eid="JOB 17:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 17:10"/>But all of them, you⁺ should return and come in, please! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:10">And I shall not find a wise one among you⁺. <verse eid="JOB 17:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 17:11"/>My days have passed by, my plans are pulled out—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:11">the possessions of my heart. <verse eid="JOB 17:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 17:12"/>They set the night into day: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:12">‘Light <char style="add">is</char> near in the face of darkness.’ <verse eid="JOB 17:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 17:13"/>If I await Sheol <char style="add">as</char> my house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:13"><char style="add">if</char> in the darkness I spread out my bed, <verse eid="JOB 17:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 17:14"/><char style="add">if</char> to the Pit I call out, ‘You are My father,’ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:14">or to the worm, ‘My mother,’ or ‘My sister’— <verse eid="JOB 17:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 17:15"/>where, then, <char style="add">is</char> my hope? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:15">And my hope, who can see it? <verse eid="JOB 17:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 17:16"/>Will <char style="add">it</char> go down into the hands of Sheol, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 17:16">if we may rest together upon the dust?” <verse eid="JOB 17:16"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 17"/>

<chapter number="18" style="c" sid="JOB 18"/>

<para style="s">Bildad: God Punishes the Wicked</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 18:1"/>Then Bildad the Shuhite answered and said: <verse eid="JOB 18:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 18:2"/>“Until when will you⁺ set snares for words? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:2">Consider, and afterward we will speak. <verse eid="JOB 18:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 18:3"/>Why are we regarded as cattle, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:3">as stopped up in your⁺ eyes? <verse eid="JOB 18:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 18:4"/>The one tearing himself in his anger—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:4">for your sake will the earth be forsaken </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:4">and the rock moved from its place? <verse eid="JOB 18:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 18:5"/>Indeed, the light of the wicked goes out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:5">and the flame of his fire does not shine. <verse eid="JOB 18:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 18:6"/>The light is dark in his tent, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:6">and his lamp above him goes out. <verse eid="JOB 18:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 18:7"/>The strides of his strength are narrowed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:7">and his counsel casts him down. <verse eid="JOB 18:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 18:8"/>For he is cast into a net by his feet, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:8">and into a mesh he walks. <verse eid="JOB 18:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 18:9"/>A trap seizes him by the heel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:9"><char style="add">and</char> a snare shall prevail over him. <verse eid="JOB 18:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 18:10"/>A cord for him is hidden in the ground, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:10">and a trap for him upon the path. <verse eid="JOB 18:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 18:11"/>Terrors round about make him tremble </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:11">and scatter him at his feet. <verse eid="JOB 18:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 18:12"/>His strength goes hungry, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:12">and destruction <char style="add">is</char> ready at his side. <verse eid="JOB 18:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 18:13"/>It devours parts of his skin; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:13">the firstborn of death devours his parts. <verse eid="JOB 18:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 18:14"/>He is torn from his tent of his safety, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:14">and is marched off to the king of terrors. <verse eid="JOB 18:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 18:15"/><char style="add">That</char> not unto him dwells in his tent; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:15">brimstone is scattered on his abode. <verse eid="JOB 18:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 18:16"/>Below, his roots are dried out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:16">and above his branch withers. <verse eid="JOB 18:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 18:17"/>His memory perishes from the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:17">and no name for him <char style="add">is</char> upon the face of the street. <verse eid="JOB 18:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 18:18"/>They drive him from light into darkness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:18">and they chase him from the world. <verse eid="JOB 18:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 18:19"/>No offspring <char style="add">is</char> unto him, and no successor among his people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:19">and no survivor in his dwellings. <verse eid="JOB 18:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 18:20"/>Those in the west are devastated at his day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:20">and those in the east are seized with horror. <verse eid="JOB 18:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 18:21"/>Surely these <char style="add">are</char> the dwellings of a perverse one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 18:21">and this <char style="add">is</char> is the place <char style="add">of one</char> who does not know God.” <verse eid="JOB 18:21"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 18"/>

<chapter number="19" style="c" sid="JOB 19"/>

<para style="s">Job: My Redeemer Lives</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 19:1"/>And Job answered and said: <verse eid="JOB 19:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 19:2"/>“Until when will you⁺ afflict my soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:2">and crush me with words? <verse eid="JOB 19:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 19:3"/>These ten times you⁺ have reproached me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:3">are you⁺ not ashamed <char style="add">that</char> you⁺ have done wrong to me? <verse eid="JOB 19:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 19:4"/>And if I have truly gone astray, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:4">my straying lodges with me. <verse eid="JOB 19:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 19:5"/>If you⁺ would truly magnify <char style="add">yourselves</char> over me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:5">and plead my reproach against me, <verse eid="JOB 19:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 19:6"/>then know that God has wronged me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:6">and has thrown His net over me. <verse eid="JOB 19:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 19:7"/>Behold, I cry out, ‘Violence!’ And I am not answered. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:7">I cry for help, <char style="add">and</char> there is no justice. <verse eid="JOB 19:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 19:8"/>My way He has walled off, and I cannot pass over; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:8">and upon my paths He has set darkness. <verse eid="JOB 19:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 19:9"/>My honor He has stripped from me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:9">and He has turned aside the crown from my head. <verse eid="JOB 19:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 19:10"/>He tears me down round about and I depart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:10">and He pulls out my hope like a tree. <verse eid="JOB 19:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 19:11"/>And He has kindled against me His anger, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:11">and He reckons me for Himself among His adversaries. <verse eid="JOB 19:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 19:12"/>His troops come as one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:12">and they build up their ramp against me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:12">and they encamp all around my tent. <verse eid="JOB 19:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 19:13"/>My brothers He has put far from me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:13">and my acquaintances surely are estranged from me. <verse eid="JOB 19:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 19:14"/>Those near to me have ceased, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:14">and those known to me have forgotten me. <verse eid="JOB 19:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 19:15"/>Those who sojourn in my house, and my maidservants, they reckon me as a stranger; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:15">I have become a foreigner in their eyes. <verse eid="JOB 19:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 19:16"/>I call to my servant, and he does not answer; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:16">with my mouth I seek favor from him. <verse eid="JOB 19:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 19:17"/>My breath is strange to my wife, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:17">and I am loathsome to the sons of my womb. <verse eid="JOB 19:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 19:18"/>Even little boys despise me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:18">I arise, and they speak against me. <verse eid="JOB 19:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 19:19"/>All the men of my counsel abhor me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:19">and those I love have turned against me. <verse eid="JOB 19:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 19:20"/>My bone clings to my skin and to my flesh, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:20">and I have escaped by the skin of my teeth. <verse eid="JOB 19:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 19:21"/>Pity me, pity me, you⁺ my friends, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:21">for the hand of God has touched me. <verse eid="JOB 19:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 19:22"/>Why do you⁺ pursue me as God <char style="add">does</char>? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:22">Are you⁺ not even satisfied with my flesh? <verse eid="JOB 19:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 19:23"/>Who will grant now that my words should be written? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:23">Who will grant <char style="add">that</char> they be inscribed in a book, <verse eid="JOB 19:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 19:24"/>with a pen of iron and with lead, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:24">they would be engraved forever in the rock! <verse eid="JOB 19:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 19:25"/>And I know <char style="add">that</char> my Redeemer<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Vindicator</char></note> lives, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:25">and in the end He will stand upon the dust.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">upon my grave</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 19:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 19:26"/>And after they strike off my skin thus, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:26">yet in my flesh<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">without my flesh</char></note> I will see God. <verse eid="JOB 19:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 19:27"/><char style="add">He</char> whom I will see for myself, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:27">indeed my eyes will see, and not a stranger. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:27">My kidneys yearn in my bosom! <verse eid="JOB 19:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 19:28"/>If you⁺ should say, ‘How we will pursue after him,’ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:28">and ‘The root of the matter is found with him,’<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Many Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, and Vulgate; most Hebrew manuscripts </char><char style="fq" closed="false">with me</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 19:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JOB 19:29"/>be afraid for yourselves of the face of the sword, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:29">for from wrath is the punishment of the sword, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 19:29">so that you⁺ may know <char style="add">there is</char> a judgment.” <verse eid="JOB 19:29"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 19"/>

<chapter number="20" style="c" sid="JOB 20"/>

<para style="s">Zophar: Destruction Awaits the Wicked</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 20:1"/>And Zophar the Naamathite answered and said: <verse eid="JOB 20:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 20:2"/>“So my anxious thoughts make me answer, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:2">because of my urgency within me. <verse eid="JOB 20:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 20:3"/>The rebuke of my shaming I have heard, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:3">and a spirit from my understanding answers for me. <verse eid="JOB 20:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 20:4"/>This do you know from long ago, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:4">from the placing of man upon the earth, <verse eid="JOB 20:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 20:5"/>that the triumph of the wicked is brief, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:5">and the rejoicing of the godless is for a moment? <verse eid="JOB 20:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 20:6"/>Though his loftiness should go up to the heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:6">and his head should touch to the clouds, <verse eid="JOB 20:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 20:7"/>like his dung, forever he will perish; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:7">those having seen him will say, ‘Where <char style="add">is</char> he?’ <verse eid="JOB 20:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 20:8"/>Like a dream he will fly away and they will not find him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:8">indeed he will be made to wander like a vision of the night. <verse eid="JOB 20:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 20:9"/>The eye <char style="add">that</char> saw him will not continue, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:9">and his place will not behold him again. <verse eid="JOB 20:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 20:10"/>His children will recompense the poor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:10">and his hands will return his wealth. <verse eid="JOB 20:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 20:11"/>His bones are full of his vigor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:11">and upon the dust it will lie down with him. <verse eid="JOB 20:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 20:12"/>Though evil is sweet in his mouth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:12"><char style="add">and</char> he hides it under his tongue, <verse eid="JOB 20:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 20:13"/>he has pity on it and does not forsake it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:13">and he withholds it in the midst of his palate. <verse eid="JOB 20:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 20:14"/>His food is turned over in his belly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:14"><char style="add">and</char> the venom of cobras <char style="add">is</char> within him. <verse eid="JOB 20:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 20:15"/>He swallows wealth and vomits it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:15">from his belly God expels it. <verse eid="JOB 20:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 20:16"/>The poison of cobras he will suck, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:16"><char style="add">and</char> the tongue of a viper will kill him. <verse eid="JOB 20:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 20:17"/>He shall not look on streams, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:17"><char style="add">or</char> rivers <char style="add">with</char> torrents of honey and cream. <verse eid="JOB 20:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 20:18"/>He will return his gain and not consume it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:18">he will not rejoice from the wealth of his exchange. <verse eid="JOB 20:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 20:19"/>For he has crushed <char style="add">and</char> forsaken the poor; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:19">he has seized a house, and he did not build it. <verse eid="JOB 20:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 20:20"/>For he has not known quiet in his belly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:20"><char style="add">and</char> with his desiring he will not deliver himself. <verse eid="JOB 20:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 20:21"/>There is no remnant for him to eat; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:21"><char style="add">and</char> upon thus his prosperity will not endure. <verse eid="JOB 20:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 20:22"/>In the fullness of his sufficiency there will be distress for him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:22">every hand of toil will come <char style="add">upon</char> him. <verse eid="JOB 20:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 20:23"/>It will come to pass at the filling of his belly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:23">that <char style="add">God</char> will send forth against him the burning of His anger, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:23">and will rain upon him into his bowels. <verse eid="JOB 20:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 20:24"/>He will flee from a weapon of iron; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:24">a bow of bronze will pierce him through. <verse eid="JOB 20:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 20:25"/>It is drawn and comes out from <char style="add">his</char> back, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:25">and the gleaming point from his gall;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from his liver</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:25">terrors shall come over him. <verse eid="JOB 20:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 20:26"/>Complete darkness is hidden for his treasuring; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:26">a fire <char style="add">that is</char> not fanned will consume him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:26">the remnant in his tent will be devoured. <verse eid="JOB 20:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 20:27"/>The heavens will uncover his iniquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:27">and the earth will rise up against him. <verse eid="JOB 20:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 20:28"/>The flood will roll away his house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:28">flowing away on the day of His anger. <verse eid="JOB 20:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JOB 20:29"/>This <char style="add">is</char> the portion of a wicked man from God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 20:29">and the heritage appointed to him from God.” <verse eid="JOB 20:29"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 20"/>

<chapter number="21" style="c" sid="JOB 21"/>

<para style="s">Job: God Will Punish the Wicked</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 21:1"/>And Job answered and said: <verse eid="JOB 21:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 21:2"/>“Listen carefully <char style="add">to</char> my speech, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:2">and let this be your⁺ consolation. <verse eid="JOB 21:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 21:3"/>Bear with me, and I will speak; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:3">and after I have spoken, you may mock. <verse eid="JOB 21:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 21:4"/>As for me, is my complaint against man? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:4">And if <char style="add">so</char>, why <char style="add">should</char> not my spirit be short? <verse eid="JOB 21:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 21:5"/>Turn to me and be appalled, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:5">and put a hand over <char style="add">your</char> mouth. <verse eid="JOB 21:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 21:6"/>Even when I remember, then I am terrified, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:6">and trembling seizes my flesh. <verse eid="JOB 21:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 21:7"/>Why do the wicked live on, growing old, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:7">even becoming mighty in power? <verse eid="JOB 21:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 21:8"/>Their seed is established with them before their face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:8">and their offspring before their eyes. <verse eid="JOB 21:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 21:9"/>Their houses <char style="add">are</char> safe from dread, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:9">and the rod of God is not upon them. <verse eid="JOB 21:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 21:10"/>His bull passes over, without fail; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:10">his cow brings forth, and <char style="add">does</char> not miscarry. <verse eid="JOB 21:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 21:11"/>They send forth their little boys like a flock, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:11">and their children skip about. <verse eid="JOB 21:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 21:12"/>They lift up to the tambourine and harp, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:12">and they rejoice at the sound of the flute. <verse eid="JOB 21:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 21:13"/>They wear out their days in prosperity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:13">and in peace<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in a moment</char></note> go down to Sheol. <verse eid="JOB 21:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 21:14"/>And they said to God, ‘Turn away from us! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:14">For we do not delight to know Your ways. <verse eid="JOB 21:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 21:15"/>What <char style="add">is</char> Shaddai<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 20</char></note> that we should serve Him? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:15">And what do we gain that we should meet with Him?’ <verse eid="JOB 21:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 21:16"/>Behold, their own good <char style="add">is</char> not in their hand; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:16">the counsel of the wicked is far from me. <verse eid="JOB 21:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 21:17"/>How often <char style="add">is</char> the lamp of the wicked put out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:17">and their destruction comes upon them? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:17">The pains He apportions in His anger. <verse eid="JOB 21:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 21:18"/>They become like straw before the face of the wind, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:18">and like chaff that the storm carries him away. <verse eid="JOB 21:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 21:19"/>Does God store up for his sons his trouble? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:19">Let Him repay to him, and he will know. <verse eid="JOB 21:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 21:20"/>Let his eyes see his destruction, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:20">and let him drink from the wrath of Shaddai. <verse eid="JOB 21:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 21:21"/>For what <char style="add">is</char> his delight in his house after him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:21">when the number of his months is cut off? <verse eid="JOB 21:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 21:22"/>Can one teach knowledge to God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:22">since He judges those being high? <verse eid="JOB 21:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 21:23"/>This one dies in the bone of his perfection, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:23">all of him at ease and at rest; <verse eid="JOB 21:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 21:24"/>his pails are full of milk, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:24">and the marrow of his bones is moist. <verse eid="JOB 21:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 21:25"/>And this one dies bitter in soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:25">and not having eaten of the good. <verse eid="JOB 21:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 21:26"/>Together upon the dust they lie down, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:26">and the worm covers them over. <verse eid="JOB 21:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 21:27"/>Behold, I know your⁺ thoughts, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:27">and the notions you⁺ wrest upon me. <verse eid="JOB 21:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 21:28"/>For you⁺ say, ‘Where <char style="add">is</char> the house of the noble? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:28">And where <char style="add">is</char> the tent of the habitation of the wicked?’ <verse eid="JOB 21:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JOB 21:29"/>Have you⁺ not asked those passing along the way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:29">and do you⁺ not recognize their signs, <verse eid="JOB 21:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JOB 21:30"/>that from a day of calamity the evil one is held back, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:30"><char style="add">and</char> in the day of wrath they are brought forth? <verse eid="JOB 21:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JOB 21:31"/>Who shall declare his way to his face? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:31">And who will repay him <char style="add">for</char> what he has done? <verse eid="JOB 21:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="JOB 21:32"/>When he is brought along to the graves, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:32">then one keeps watch over <char style="add">his</char> tomb. <verse eid="JOB 21:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="JOB 21:33"/>The clods of the torrent are sweet to him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:33">and after him every man will extend, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:33">and those before his face are without number. <verse eid="JOB 21:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="JOB 21:34"/>And how can you⁺ comfort me in vain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 21:34">and in your⁺ answers remains falsehood?” <verse eid="JOB 21:34"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 21"/>

<chapter number="22" style="c" sid="JOB 22"/>

<para style="s">Eliphaz: Can a Man Be of Use to God?</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 22:1"/>And Eliphaz the Temanite answered and said: <verse eid="JOB 22:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 22:2"/>“Can a man be useful to God? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:2">Can even a wise one benefit Him? <verse eid="JOB 22:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 22:3"/>Is it pleasure to Shaddai<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 17, 23, 25, and 26</char></note> that you are righteous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:3">or gain that you perfect your ways? <verse eid="JOB 22:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 22:4"/>For your fear does He rebuke you </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:4">and enter against you into judgment? <verse eid="JOB 22:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 22:5"/>Is not your evil great, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:5">and your iniquity without end? <verse eid="JOB 22:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 22:6"/>For you take a pledge from your brothers needlessly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:6">and the garments the naked you strip off. <verse eid="JOB 22:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 22:7"/>You have not quenched with water the weary, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:7">and from the hungry you have withheld bread. <verse eid="JOB 22:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 22:8"/>But the man of arm, unto him <char style="add">is</char> the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:8">and the uplifted of face, he dwells in it! <verse eid="JOB 22:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 22:9"/>You have sent away widows in emptiness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:9">and the arms of the fatherless are crushed. <verse eid="JOB 22:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 22:10"/>Upon thus <char style="add">there are</char> snares all around you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:10">and dread suddenly terrifies you, <verse eid="JOB 22:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 22:11"/>or darkness you cannot see, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:11">and an abundance of waters covers you. <verse eid="JOB 22:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 22:12"/>Is not God in the height of the heavens? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:12">And behold, the head of the stars, how exalted they are! <verse eid="JOB 22:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 22:13"/>And you say, ‘What does God know? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:13"><char style="add">How</char> can He judge through the dark cloud? <verse eid="JOB 22:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 22:14"/>Clouds are a covering for Him, so that He does not see, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:14">and the vault of the heavens<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">heaven’s horizon</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the circle of the sky</char></note> He walks about.’ <verse eid="JOB 22:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 22:15"/>Will you keep the way of old, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:15">which men of iniquity have trod, <verse eid="JOB 22:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 22:16"/>who were seized, and <char style="add">it was</char> not time, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:16">their foundation was poured out <char style="add">by</char> a torrent? <verse eid="JOB 22:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 22:17"/>They said to God, ‘Turn away from us!’ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:17">And’What can Shaddai do to <char style="add">us</char>?’ <verse eid="JOB 22:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 22:18"/>Yet He filled their houses <char style="add">with</char> good—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:18">and the counsel of the wicked, may it be far from me! <verse eid="JOB 22:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 22:19"/>The righteous see <char style="add">it</char> and are glad, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:19">and the innocent one mocks them: <verse eid="JOB 22:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 22:20"/>‘Surely our adversaries cut off, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:20">and fire consumes their excess.’ <verse eid="JOB 22:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 22:21"/>Make yourself of use now, and be at peace with Him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:21">with these <char style="add">things</char> will come to you good. <verse eid="JOB 22:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 22:22"/>Receive, please, instruction from His mouth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:22">and set His words in your heart. <verse eid="JOB 22:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 22:23"/>If you should return to Shaddai, you will be built up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:23"><char style="add">if</char> you put far away from your tent iniquity, <verse eid="JOB 22:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 22:24"/>and <char style="add">if</char> you set your gold upon the dust, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:24">and Ophir among the stones of the torrents, <verse eid="JOB 22:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 22:25"/>then Shaddai will be your gold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:25">and the silver of heights for you. <verse eid="JOB 22:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 22:26"/>For then you will take delight in Shaddai, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:26">and you will lift to God your face. <verse eid="JOB 22:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 22:27"/>You will pray to Him, and He will hear you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:27">and your vows you will fulfill. <verse eid="JOB 22:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 22:28"/>Then you will decree a word, and it will stand for you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:28">and upon your paths light will shine. <verse eid="JOB 22:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JOB 22:29"/>When they have made low, and you say Lift up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:29">then the lowly of eyes He will save. <verse eid="JOB 22:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JOB 22:30"/>He will deliver the one not innocent, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 22:30">rescuing him by the purity of your hands.” <verse eid="JOB 22:30"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 22"/>

<chapter number="23" style="c" sid="JOB 23"/>

<para style="s">Job Longs for God</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 23:1"/>And Job answered and said: <verse eid="JOB 23:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 23:2"/>“Even this day my complaint is bitter; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:2">my hand is heavy upon my groaning. <verse eid="JOB 23:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 23:3"/>Who will grant <char style="add">that</char> I might know and find Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:3"><char style="add">and</char> come unto His seat! <verse eid="JOB 23:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 23:4"/>I would set forth to his face my case, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:4">and my mouth I would fill <char style="add">with</char> arguments. <verse eid="JOB 23:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 23:5"/>I would know the words He would answer me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:5">and I would understand what He would say to me. <verse eid="JOB 23:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 23:6"/>In the abundance of strength would He contend with me? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:6">No, surely He would set <char style="add">it</char> upon me. <verse eid="JOB 23:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 23:7"/>There the upright could argue with Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:7">and I would escape forever from the One judging me. <verse eid="JOB 23:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 23:8"/>Behold, east I go, and He is not there, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:8">and west, and I do not perceive Him. <verse eid="JOB 23:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 23:9"/>In the north, in His working, I do not behold <char style="add">Him</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:9">He turns to the south, and I do not see <char style="add">Him</char>. <verse eid="JOB 23:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 23:10"/>Yet He knows the way with me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:10">He has tested me, <char style="add">and</char> like gold I will come forth. <verse eid="JOB 23:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 23:11"/>My foot has held firm by His steps; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:11">His way I have kept, and I have not turned aside. <verse eid="JOB 23:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 23:12"/>And I have not departed from the commandment of His lips; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:12">more than my portion I have treasured the words of His mouth. <verse eid="JOB 23:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 23:13"/>And He is of one, and who can turn Him back? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:13">And His soul has desired, and He has done. <verse eid="JOB 23:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 23:14"/>For He carries out <char style="add">what is</char> appointed for me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:14">and many like these <char style="add">are</char> with Him. <verse eid="JOB 23:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 23:15"/>Upon thus, I am terrified before His face; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:15">I consider <char style="add">this</char>, and I am afraid of Him. <verse eid="JOB 23:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 23:16"/>And God has softened my heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:16">and Shaddai has terrified me. <verse eid="JOB 23:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 23:17"/>For I was not cut off from the face of darkness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 23:17">and before my face He has covered the dark gloom. </para>

<para style="p" vid="JOB 23:17"> <char style="add">Shaddai</char> means <char style="add">the Almighty</char><verse eid="JOB 23:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 23"/>

<chapter number="24" style="c" sid="JOB 24"/>

<para style="s">Job: Judgment for the Wicked</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 24:1"/><char style="add">“</char> Why from Shaddai are the times not hidden away, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:1">and those knowing Him, they have not seen His days? <verse eid="JOB 24:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 24:2"/>They move boundary markers; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:2">they seize a flock and pasture it. <verse eid="JOB 24:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 24:3"/>They drive away the donkey of the fatherless; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:3">they take as a pledge the ox of the widow. <verse eid="JOB 24:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 24:4"/>They push the needy off the road; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:4">together are hidden the poor of the land. <verse eid="JOB 24:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 24:5"/>Behold, wild donkeys in the desert, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:5">they go forth in their work of searching for food; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:5">the Arabah <char style="add">gives</char> food for them <char style="add">and</char> for the young. <verse eid="JOB 24:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 24:6"/>In the field they gather his fodder, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:6">and in the vineyard of the wicked they glean. <verse eid="JOB 24:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 24:7"/>Naked they spend the night without a garment, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:7">and with no covering in the cold. <verse eid="JOB 24:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 24:8"/>From the showers of the mountains they are wet, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:8">and from <char style="add">being</char> without a shelter, they have embraced the rock. <verse eid="JOB 24:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 24:9"/>They snatch from the breast the fatherless, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:9">and the suckling of the poor they bind with a pledge. <verse eid="JOB 24:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 24:10"/>Naked They go about, without clothing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:10">and hungry—they carry a sheaf. <verse eid="JOB 24:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 24:11"/>Between their walls they press oil; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:11">they tread the winepresses and go thirsty. <verse eid="JOB 24:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 24:12"/>From the city men groan, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:12">and the souls of the wounded cry out; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:12">yet God does not ascribe impropriety. <verse eid="JOB 24:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 24:13"/>They are among those rebelling against the light; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:13">they do not recognize its ways, and they do not dwell in its paths. <verse eid="JOB 24:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 24:14"/>At light the murderer arises; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:14">he kills the poor and needy, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:14">and in the night he is like a thief. <verse eid="JOB 24:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 24:15"/>And the eye of the adulterer watches for twilight, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:15">saying, ‘No eye will see me,’ and he puts a cover over his face. <verse eid="JOB 24:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 24:16"/>In the darkness one digs <char style="add">into</char> houses, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:16">by day they seal themselves in; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:16">they do not know the light. <verse eid="JOB 24:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 24:17"/>For the morning <char style="add">is</char> for them together the shadow of death—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:17">for one regards the terrors of the shadow of death! <verse eid="JOB 24:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 24:18"/>He is swift on the face of the waters; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:18">cursed <char style="add">is</char> their portion in the land. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:18">He does not turn to the way of the vineyards. <verse eid="JOB 24:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 24:19"/><char style="add">As</char> drought and heat tear away the waters of snow, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:19"><char style="add">so</char> Sheol <char style="add">does</char> to those who have sinned. <verse eid="JOB 24:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 24:20"/>The womb forgets him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:20">the worm feeds sweetly on him; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 24:20">no more is he remembered, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:20">and injustice is broken like a tree. <verse eid="JOB 24:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 24:21"/>For he feeds <char style="add">on</char> the barren woman <char style="add">who</char> cannot give birth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:21">and <char style="add">to</char> the widow he does not do good. <verse eid="JOB 24:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 24:22"/>And he draws away the mighty with his power; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:22">he rises up, and he is not sure of life. <verse eid="JOB 24:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 24:23"/>He gives to him security, and he is supported; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:23">and his eyes <char style="add">are</char> on their ways. <verse eid="JOB 24:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 24:24"/>They are exalted for a little <char style="add">while</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:24">then they <char style="add">are</char> no more; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 24:24">and they are brought low like all <char style="add">and</char> are gathered up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:24">and like heads of grain they wither. <verse eid="JOB 24:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 24:25"/>And if not, then who will prove me a liar, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 24:25">and set to nought my speech?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="JOB 24:25"> <char style="add">Shaddai</char> means <char style="add">the Almighty</char><verse eid="JOB 24:25"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 24"/>

<chapter number="25" style="c" sid="JOB 25"/>

<para style="s">Bildad: Man Cannot Be Righteous</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 25:1"/>And Bildad the Shuhite answered and said: <verse eid="JOB 25:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 25:2"/>“Dominion and dread <char style="add">are</char> with Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 25:2">the One making peace in His high places. <verse eid="JOB 25:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 25:3"/>Is there a number to His troops? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 25:3">And upon whom does His light not arise? <verse eid="JOB 25:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 25:4"/>So how can a man be righteous with God? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 25:4">Or what can be pure <char style="add">that</char> is born of a woman? <verse eid="JOB 25:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 25:5"/>Behold, even the moon does not shine, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 25:5">and the stars are not pure in His eyes. <verse eid="JOB 25:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 25:6"/>How much less a man—a maggot, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 25:6">and a son of man—a worm!” <verse eid="JOB 25:6"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 25"/>

<chapter number="26" style="c" sid="JOB 26"/>

<para style="s">Job: Who Can Understand God’s Majesty?</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 26:1"/>And Job answered and said: <verse eid="JOB 26:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 26:2"/>“How you have helped the one without power! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 26:2">You have saved the arm <char style="add">with</char> no strength! <verse eid="JOB 26:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 26:3"/>How you have advised one without wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 26:3">and have made known insight in abundance! <verse eid="JOB 26:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 26:4"/>With whom have you declared <char style="add">these</char> words? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 26:4">And whose breath has come forth from you? <verse eid="JOB 26:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 26:5"/>The dead are writhing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 26:5">underneath the waters and those inhabiting them. <verse eid="JOB 26:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 26:6"/>Naked <char style="add">is</char> Sheol before Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 26:6">and there is no covering to Abaddon.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Abaddon</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Destruction</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 26:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 26:7"/>He stretches out Zaphon over the void, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 26:7">hanging the earth on nothing whatsoever. <verse eid="JOB 26:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 26:8"/>Binding the waters in His thick clouds, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 26:8">and the clouds are not broken apart under them, <verse eid="JOB 26:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 26:9"/>He covers the face of the throne,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of the full moon</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 26:9"><char style="add">and</char> spreads over it His cloud. <verse eid="JOB 26:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 26:10"/>He has circled a limit upon the face of the waters, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 26:10">to <char style="add">be</char> the boundary of light with darkness. <verse eid="JOB 26:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 26:11"/>The pillars of the heavens tremble </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 26:11">and are astonished at his rebuke. <verse eid="JOB 26:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 26:12"/>By His strength He stirred<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">stilled</char></note> the Sea, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 26:12">and by His understanding He shattered Rahab. <verse eid="JOB 26:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 26:13"/>By His breath the heavens were made clear; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 26:13">His hand pierced the fleeing serpent.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">nachash</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; translated in most cases as </char><char style="fq" closed="false">snake</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 26:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 26:14"/>Behold, these are the edges of His ways, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 26:14">and how faint of a word do we hear of Him! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 26:14">And the thundering of His might, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 26:14">who can understand?” <verse eid="JOB 26:14"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 26"/>

<chapter number="27" style="c" sid="JOB 27"/>

<para style="s">Job Affirms His Integrity</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 27:1"/>And Job proceeded again to take up his discourse, and he said, <verse eid="JOB 27:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 27:2"/>“<char style="add">As</char> God lives, <char style="add">who</char> has turned aside my justice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:2">and Shaddai <char style="add">who</char> has embittered my soul— <verse eid="JOB 27:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 27:3"/>that any of my breath still <char style="add">is</char> in me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:3">and the breath of God <char style="add">is</char> in my nostrils, <verse eid="JOB 27:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 27:4"/>my lips will not speak wickedness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:4">and my tongue will not utter deceit. <verse eid="JOB 27:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 27:5"/>Far be it from me that I justify you⁺; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:5">until I die, I will not turn aside my integrity from me. <verse eid="JOB 27:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 27:6"/>My righteousness I hold fast, and I will not let go; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:6">my heart shall not reproach <char style="add">me</char> in my days. <verse eid="JOB 27:6"/></para>

<para style="s">The Wicked Man’s Portion</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 27:7"/>May my enemy be like the wicked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:7">and the one rising up against me like the unjust. <verse eid="JOB 27:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 27:8"/>For what is the hope of the godless when he is cut off, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:8">when God takes away his life? <verse eid="JOB 27:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 27:9"/>Will God hear his cry </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:9">when distress comes upon him? <verse eid="JOB 27:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 27:10"/>Indeed will he delight himself upon Shaddai? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:10">Will he call upon God at any time? <verse eid="JOB 27:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 27:11"/>I will teach you⁺ about the hand of God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:11">that which <char style="add">is</char> with Shaddai I will not hide. <verse eid="JOB 27:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 27:12"/>Behold, you⁺—all of you⁺—you⁺ have seen this; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:12">why then do you⁺ vainly utter this vanity? <verse eid="JOB 27:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 27:13"/>This <char style="add">is</char> the portion of the wicked man with God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:13">and the inheritance of the ruthless <char style="add">which</char> they receive from Shaddai. <verse eid="JOB 27:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 27:14"/>If his sons should increase, <char style="add">it is</char> for the sword; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:14">and his offspring shall not be satisfied <char style="add">with</char> bread. <verse eid="JOB 27:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 27:15"/>His survivor will be buried in death, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:15">and his widows will not lament. <verse eid="JOB 27:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 27:16"/>Though he heaps up silver like the dust, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:16">and piles up clothing like the clay, <verse eid="JOB 27:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 27:17"/>he may pile <char style="add">it</char> up, but the righteous will wear <char style="add">it</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:17">and the innocent will divide <char style="add">his</char> silver. <verse eid="JOB 27:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 27:18"/>He builds his house like the moth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:18">and like a booth made <char style="add">by</char> a watchman. <verse eid="JOB 27:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 27:19"/>He lies down rich, but he shall not gather again; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:19">he opens his eyes, and he is not. <verse eid="JOB 27:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 27:20"/>Terrors overwhelm him like waters; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:20">in the night a tempest steals him away. <verse eid="JOB 27:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 27:21"/>The east wind carries him away, and he is gone; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:21">and it sweeps him from his place. <verse eid="JOB 27:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 27:22"/>And it hurls <char style="add">itself</char> upon him, and does not spare; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:22">he urgently flees from its hand. <verse eid="JOB 27:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 27:23"/>It claps its hands at him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 27:23">and hisses at him from his place. </para>

<para style="p" vid="JOB 27:23"> <char style="add">Shaddai</char> means <char style="add">the Almighty</char>; also in verses 10, 11, and 13<verse eid="JOB 27:23"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 27"/>

<chapter number="28" style="c" sid="JOB 28"/>

<para style="s">Where Can Wisdom Be Found?</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 28:1"/><char style="add">“</char> Surely there is a mine for silver, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:1">and a place for the gold <char style="add">that</char> they refine. <verse eid="JOB 28:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 28:2"/>Iron is taken from the dust, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:2">and <char style="add">from</char> rock copper is smelted. <verse eid="JOB 28:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 28:3"/>An end he has set for the darkness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:3">yet to every limit he is searching out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:3">a stone in darkness and the shadow of death. <verse eid="JOB 28:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 28:4"/>He opens a shaft away from habitation; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:4">those forgotten by the foot, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:4">they hang down away from man, and they sway. <verse eid="JOB 28:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 28:5"/>The earth, from which bread comes forth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:5">and underneath is turned as <char style="add">by</char> fire— <verse eid="JOB 28:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 28:6"/>a place of sapphire <char style="add">are</char> its stones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:6">and dust of gold <char style="add">is</char> unto it. <verse eid="JOB 28:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 28:7"/>The path no bird of prey knows, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:7">and no eye of a falcon has seen it. <verse eid="JOB 28:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 28:8"/>The sons of pride have not trodden it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:8">and the lion has not passed over it. <verse eid="JOB 28:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 28:9"/>Against the flinty rock he stretched out his hand; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:9">he overturns the hills from the root. <verse eid="JOB 28:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 28:10"/>In the rocks he cuts out channels, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:10">and his eye sees every precious thing. <verse eid="JOB 28:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 28:11"/>The rivers he has bound from weeping,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew; LXX and Vulgate </char><char style="fq" closed="false">he has laid bare the depths of rivers</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:11">and a hidden thing he brings to light. <verse eid="JOB 28:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 28:12"/>And wisdom—from where is it found? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:12">And where <char style="add">is</char> this place of understanding? <verse eid="JOB 28:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 28:13"/>Man does not know its value, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:13">and it is not found in the land of the living. <verse eid="JOB 28:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 28:14"/>The deep says, ‘It <char style="add">is</char> not in me,’ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:14">and the sea says, ‘It is not with me.’ <verse eid="JOB 28:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 28:15"/>Gold cannot be given for it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:15">nor can silver be weighed <char style="add">for</char> its price. <verse eid="JOB 28:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 28:16"/>It is not valued with the gold of Ophir, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:16">with precious onyx or sapphire. <verse eid="JOB 28:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 28:17"/>Gold and crystal cannot equal it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:17">or <char style="add">is</char> its exchange a vessel of fine gold. <verse eid="JOB 28:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 28:18"/>Coral and quartz <char style="add">are</char> not to be mentioned; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:18">and the acquisition of wisdom is more than rubies. <verse eid="JOB 28:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 28:19"/>The topaz of Cush<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the upper Nile region</char></note> cannot equal it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:19">nor it is valued in pure gold. <verse eid="JOB 28:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 28:20"/>And the wisdom, from where does it come? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:20">And where <char style="add">is</char> this place of understanding? <verse eid="JOB 28:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 28:21"/>And is it hidden from the eyes of every living <char style="add">thing</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:21">even from the birds of the heavens it is concealed. <verse eid="JOB 28:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 28:22"/>Abaddon<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Abaddon</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Destruction</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> and Death say, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:22">‘We have heard a report of it with our ears.’ <verse eid="JOB 28:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 28:23"/>God has understood its way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:23">and He has known its place. <verse eid="JOB 28:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 28:24"/>For He looks to the ends of the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:24"><char style="add">and</char> He sees under all the heavens, <verse eid="JOB 28:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 28:25"/>to make for the wind a weight, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:25">and He portioned out the waters by measure, <verse eid="JOB 28:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 28:26"/>in His making a limit for the rain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:26">and a path for the flash of the thunders— <verse eid="JOB 28:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 28:27"/>then He saw and recounted it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:27">He established it and also searched it out. <verse eid="JOB 28:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 28:28"/>And He said to the man, ‘Behold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:28">the fear of the Lord—that <char style="add">is</char> wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 28:28">and the turning aside from evil <char style="add">is</char> understanding.’” <verse eid="JOB 28:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 28"/>

<chapter number="29" style="c" sid="JOB 29"/>

<para style="s">Job’s Former Blessings</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 29:1"/>And Job continued to lift up his discourse, and he said, <verse eid="JOB 29:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 29:2"/>“Who will make me as <char style="add">in</char> months past, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:2">as the days <char style="add">when</char> God was keeping me? <verse eid="JOB 29:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 29:3"/>In His lamp shining upon my head, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:3">by His light I walked <char style="add">through</char> darkness, <verse eid="JOB 29:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 29:4"/>as I was in the days of my harvest time,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">29.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in my prime</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:4">when the counsel of God was upon my tent, <verse eid="JOB 29:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 29:5"/>when yet Shaddai<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">29.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char></note> <char style="add">was</char> with me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:5">my children around me, <verse eid="JOB 29:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 29:6"/>with the washing of my steps with cream, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:6">and the rock poured out for me streams of oil! <verse eid="JOB 29:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 29:7"/><char style="add">Or</char> in my going out <char style="add">to</char> the gate upon the town, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:7">in the square I established my seat; <verse eid="JOB 29:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 29:8"/>the young men saw me and hid themselves, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:8">and old men arose <char style="add">and</char> stood; <verse eid="JOB 29:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 29:9"/>the princes refrained from words, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:9">and they put a hand on their mouth; <verse eid="JOB 29:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 29:10"/>the voice of the nobles was hidden, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:10">and their tongue stuck to their palate. <verse eid="JOB 29:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 29:11"/>For the ear heard and declared me blessed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:11">and the eye saw and testified for me, <verse eid="JOB 29:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 29:12"/>because I rescued the poor crying out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:12">and the fatherless, and no one was helping him. <verse eid="JOB 29:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 29:13"/>The blessing of the one perishing came upon me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:13">and the heart of the widow I caused to sing. <verse eid="JOB 29:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 29:14"/>I clothed myself with righteousness, and it clothed me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:14">like a robe and a turban <char style="add">was</char> my justice. <verse eid="JOB 29:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 29:15"/>I was eyes to the blind, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:15">and I <char style="add">was</char> feet to the lame. <verse eid="JOB 29:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 29:16"/>I <char style="add">was</char> a father to the poor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:16">and the case I did not know, I searched it out. <verse eid="JOB 29:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 29:17"/>And I broke the fangs of the unjust, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:17">and I cast away the prey from his teeth. <verse eid="JOB 29:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 29:18"/>So I said, ‘In my nest I will die, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:18">I will multiply <char style="add">my</char> days as the sand. <verse eid="JOB 29:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 29:19"/>My root is open to the waters, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:19">and the dew lodges on my branch. <verse eid="JOB 29:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 29:20"/>My glory <char style="add">is</char> fresh within me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:20">and my bow in my hand is renewed.’ <verse eid="JOB 29:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 29:21"/>They listened to me and waited, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:21">and they kept silent for my counsel. <verse eid="JOB 29:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 29:22"/>After my word, they did not speak again, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:22">and my speech dripped upon them. <verse eid="JOB 29:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 29:23"/>And they waited for me as for the rain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:23">and their mouth they opened wide, as for the spring rain. <verse eid="JOB 29:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 29:24"/>I smiled at them, <char style="add">and</char> they could not believe <char style="add">it</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:24">and the light of my face they did not let fall. <verse eid="JOB 29:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 29:25"/>I chose their path and sat <char style="add">as</char> chief, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:25">and I dwelt as a king with <char style="add">his</char> band, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 29:25">like one who comforts the mourners. <verse eid="JOB 29:25"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 29"/>

<chapter number="30" style="c" sid="JOB 30"/>

<para style="s">Job’s Honor Turned to Contempt</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 30:1"/><char style="add">“</char> And now they laugh at me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:1">the fewer in days than I, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 30:1">whose fathers I disdained </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:1">to put with the dogs of my flock. <verse eid="JOB 30:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 30:2"/>Indeed, the strength of their hands, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:2">what <char style="add">is it</char> to me? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:2">Upon them vigor has perished, <verse eid="JOB 30:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 30:3"/>in poverty and in harsh hunger, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:3">ones gnawing the dry ground by night, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:3"><char style="add">in</char> ruin and desolation. <verse eid="JOB 30:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 30:4"/>They <char style="add">are</char> plucking mallow among the brush, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:4">and the root of the broom tree is their bread.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">their fuel</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 30:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 30:5"/>From the midst of people they are driven out; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:5">they shout at them as <char style="add">at</char> a thief. <verse eid="JOB 30:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 30:6"/>On the slope of wadis <char style="add">they are</char> to dwell, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:6">in holes of the dust and rocks. <verse eid="JOB 30:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 30:7"/>Among the shrubs they bray; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:7">under the nettles they huddle together. <verse eid="JOB 30:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 30:8"/>Sons of a fool, even sons without a name, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:8">they were scourged from the land. <verse eid="JOB 30:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 30:9"/>And now I have become their song, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:9">and I have become a byword among them. <verse eid="JOB 30:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 30:10"/>They abhor me <char style="add">and</char> keep far from me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:10">and from my face they do not withhold spit. <verse eid="JOB 30:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 30:11"/>For my bowstring he has loosed and afflicted me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:11">and they have cast <char style="add">off</char> the bridle before me. <verse eid="JOB 30:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 30:12"/>On the right a brood arises; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:12">they push away my feet, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:12">and they build up against me the ways of destruction. <verse eid="JOB 30:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 30:13"/>They break up my path; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:13">they advance my calamity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:13">with no one helping them.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">with no one restraining them</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 30:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 30:14"/>As a wide breach they come; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:14">amid the ruin they roll on. <verse eid="JOB 30:14"/></para>

<para style="s">Job’s Prosperity Becomes Calamity</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 30:15"/>Terrors are turned over upon me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:15">like the wind it pursues my honor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:15">and like a cloud my deliverance has passed away. <verse eid="JOB 30:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 30:16"/>And now within me my soul is poured out; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:16">days of affliction seize me. <verse eid="JOB 30:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 30:17"/>Night pierces my bones from upon me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:17">and my gnawing pains will not lie down. <verse eid="JOB 30:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 30:18"/>With abundance of strength He grasps my garment;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">my garment is disfigured</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:18">by the collar of my tunic He seizes me. <verse eid="JOB 30:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 30:19"/>He has cast me into the mire, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:19">and I have become like dust and ashes. <verse eid="JOB 30:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 30:20"/>I cry out to You, but You do not answer me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:20">I stand up, and You gaze at me. <verse eid="JOB 30:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 30:21"/>You have turned to <char style="add">be</char> cruel toward me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:21">with the strength of Your hand You oppose me. <verse eid="JOB 30:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 30:22"/>You lift me up to the wind </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:22">and make me ride <char style="add">it</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:22">You toss me about<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">You dissolve me</char></note> in the storm. <verse eid="JOB 30:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 30:23"/>For I know <char style="add">that</char> You will bring me <char style="add">to</char> death, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:23">and <char style="add">to</char> the house of appointment to all the living. <verse eid="JOB 30:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 30:24"/>Surely one does not stretch out a hand against the oppressed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:24">when in his ruin he cries out to <char style="add">him</char>. <verse eid="JOB 30:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 30:25"/>If not did I weep for the harshness of day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:25"><char style="add">while</char> my soul grieved for the needy one? <verse eid="JOB 30:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 30:26"/>And, I hoped for good, and evil came; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:26">and I waited for light, and darkness came. <verse eid="JOB 30:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 30:27"/>My bowels have boiled and they do not rest; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:27">days of affliction confront me. <verse eid="JOB 30:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 30:28"/>I go about darkened, not by the sun; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:28">I rise up in the assembly <char style="add">and</char> cry out. <verse eid="JOB 30:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JOB 30:29"/>I have become a brother to jackals,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">serpents</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">dragons</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:29">and a companion to the daughters of the ostrich.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the daughters of the owl</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 30:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JOB 30:30"/>My skin turns black and falls from me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:30">and my bone burns with heat. <verse eid="JOB 30:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JOB 30:31"/>And my harp is changed to mourning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 30:31">and my flute to the voice of weeping. <verse eid="JOB 30:31"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 30"/>

<chapter number="31" style="c" sid="JOB 31"/>

<para style="s">Job’s Final Appeal</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 31:1"/><char style="add">“</char> I have made A covenant with my eyes; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:1">and how could I gaze upon a virgin? <verse eid="JOB 31:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 31:2"/>For what would be the portion of God from above, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:2">and the inheritance of Shaddai<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">31.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 35</char></note> in the heights? <verse eid="JOB 31:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 31:3"/>Is not disaster for the perverse one </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:3">and calamity for the workers of iniquity? <verse eid="JOB 31:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 31:4"/>Does He not see my ways, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:4">and count all my steps? <verse eid="JOB 31:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 31:5"/>If I have walked with falsehood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:5">and my foot has hurried toward deceit, <verse eid="JOB 31:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 31:6"/>let Him weigh me in the scales of justice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:6">and let God know my integrity. <verse eid="JOB 31:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 31:7"/>If my step has turned aside from the way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:7">and my heart has walked, following my eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:7">and on my palms has stuck a spot, <verse eid="JOB 31:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 31:8"/><char style="add">then</char> let me sow, and another may eat, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:8">and may my crops be uprooted! <verse eid="JOB 31:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 31:9"/>If my heart has been enticed over a woman, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:9">or I have lain in wait at the door of my neighbor, <verse eid="JOB 31:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 31:10"/><char style="add">then</char> let my wife grind for another, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:10">and others bend down over her. <verse eid="JOB 31:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 31:11"/>For it <char style="add">is</char> wickedness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:11">and it <char style="add">is</char> to be judged an iniquity. <verse eid="JOB 31:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 31:12"/>For it is a fire <char style="add">that</char> devours unto Abaddon,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">31.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Abaddon</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Destruction</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:12">and it would uproot among all my produce. <verse eid="JOB 31:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 31:13"/>If I have rejected the justice of my manservant or my maidservant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:13">in their dispute with me, <verse eid="JOB 31:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 31:14"/>then what shall I do when God arises? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:14">And when He inspects, how shall I answer him? <verse eid="JOB 31:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 31:15"/>Did not the One making me in the belly make them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:15">and <char style="add">that</char> One prepare us in the womb? <verse eid="JOB 31:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 31:16"/>If I have withheld the poor from pleasure </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:16">and made to fail the eyes of the widow, <verse eid="JOB 31:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 31:17"/>and have eaten my morsel alone, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:17">and the fatherless could not eat from it— <verse eid="JOB 31:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 31:18"/>indeed from my youth I brought him up as a father, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:18">and from the womb of my mother I guided her— <verse eid="JOB 31:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 31:19"/>if I have seen one perishing from lack of clothing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:19">or there <char style="add">being</char> no covering for the needy, <verse eid="JOB 31:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 31:20"/>if his loins have not blessed me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:20">for warming him by the fleece of my sheep, <verse eid="JOB 31:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 31:21"/>if I have raised my hand against the fatherless, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:21">because I saw my help at the gate, <verse eid="JOB 31:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 31:22"/><char style="add">then</char> let my upper arm fall from its shoulder, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:22">and my arm be broken <char style="add">off</char> from its socket. <verse eid="JOB 31:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 31:23"/>For a calamity from God <char style="add">is</char> dread to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:23">and His majesty I cannot overpower. <verse eid="JOB 31:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 31:24"/>If I have set my confidence <char style="add">upon</char> gold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:24">or to fine gold I have said, “My trust;” <verse eid="JOB 31:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 31:25"/>if I have rejoiced because my wealth <char style="add">was</char> great, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:25">and because my hand had acquired much; <verse eid="JOB 31:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 31:26"/>if I have seen the light<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">31.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the sun</char></note> when it shines, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:26">or the moon moving <char style="add">in</char> splendor, <verse eid="JOB 31:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 31:27"/>so that my heart has been enticed in secret, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:27">and my hand has kissed my mouth, <verse eid="JOB 31:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 31:28"/><char style="add">then</char> this also be judged an iniquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:28">for I would have lied to God above. <verse eid="JOB 31:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JOB 31:29"/>If I have rejoiced in the destruction of one hating me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:29">or raised myself up because evil found him— <verse eid="JOB 31:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JOB 31:30"/>though I had not given my mouth to sin </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:30">by asking with a curse for his life— <verse eid="JOB 31:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JOB 31:31"/>if the men of my tent have not said, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:31">‘Who will give from his flesh not having been satisfied?’— <verse eid="JOB 31:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="JOB 31:32"/>A sojourner does not lodge in the street, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:32"><char style="add">for</char> I have opened my doors to the traveler— <verse eid="JOB 31:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="JOB 31:33"/>if I have covered my transgressions like Adam,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">31.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">like men</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:33">by hiding my guilt in my bosom, <verse eid="JOB 31:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="JOB 31:34"/>because I feared the great multitude, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:34">and the contempt of the clans terrified me </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 31:34">and I kept silent, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:34">not going out the door— <verse eid="JOB 31:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="JOB 31:35"/>(Who will give to me one listening to me? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:35">Behold, my mark </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 31:35">and let Shaddai answer me! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:35">And the bill the man of my dispute that has written! <verse eid="JOB 31:35"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="JOB 31:36"/>If not, I would take it up upon my shoulder, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:36"><char style="add">and</char> bind it as crowns to myself. <verse eid="JOB 31:36"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="JOB 31:37"/>The count of my steps I would declare to him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:37">like a prince I would approach Him.)— <verse eid="JOB 31:37"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="JOB 31:38"/>If my land cries out against me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:38">and together its furrows weep; <verse eid="JOB 31:38"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="JOB 31:39"/>if I have eaten its power without silver, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:39">and I have caused to breathe out the soul of its workers, <verse eid="JOB 31:39"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="JOB 31:40"/><char style="add">then</char> in place of the wheat let a thorn come forth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 31:40">and weeds in place of barley.” </para>

<para style="p" vid="JOB 31:40">The words of Job have ended. <verse eid="JOB 31:40"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 31"/>

<chapter number="32" style="c" sid="JOB 32"/>

<para style="s">Elihu Rebukes Job’s Friends</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 32:1"/>And these three men ceased from answering Job, because he <char style="add">was</char> righteous in his own eyes. <verse eid="JOB 32:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 32:2"/>But the anger of Elihu son of Barachel, the Buzite from the family of Ram, was kindled; his anger was kindled against Job, upon his justifying himself rather than God. <verse eid="JOB 32:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 32:3"/>And his anger was kindled against his three friends, upon that they had not found an answer, and they had declared Job wrong. <verse eid="JOB 32:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 32:4"/>And Elihu had waited with words <char style="add">to</char> Job, because they <char style="add">were</char> older than he in days. <verse eid="JOB 32:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 32:5"/>And Elihu saw that there was no answer in the mouth of the three men, and his anger was kindled. <verse eid="JOB 32:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 32:6"/>And Elihu son of Barachel the Buzite answered and said, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 32:6">“I <char style="add">am</char> Young in days, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:6">and you⁺ <char style="add">are</char> aged; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 32:6">upon thus I shrank back, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:6">and I was afraid of declaring my knowledge to you⁺. <verse eid="JOB 32:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 32:7"/>I said, “Days shall speak, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:7">and a multitude of years shall make known wisdom.’ <verse eid="JOB 32:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 32:8"/>Surely it <char style="add">is</char> a spirit<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">32.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Spirit</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; similarly in verse 18</char></note> in a man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:8">and the breath of Shaddai<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">32.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char></note> gives them understanding. <verse eid="JOB 32:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 32:9"/>Not <char style="add">only</char> the great <char style="add">in years</char> <char style="add">are</char> wise, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:9">nor do <char style="add">only</char> the aged understand justice. <verse eid="JOB 32:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 32:10"/>Therefore I say, ‘Listen to me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:10">I will declare my knowledge, even I.’ <verse eid="JOB 32:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 32:11"/>Behold, I have waited for your⁺ words; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:11">I gave <char style="add">my</char> ear to your⁺ reasonings, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 32:11">while you⁺ searched for the words. <verse eid="JOB 32:11"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 32:12"/>And to you⁺ I attended, and behold, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 32:12">there was no one proving Job wrong </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:12"><char style="add">or</char> answering his words among you⁺, <verse eid="JOB 32:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 32:13"/>lest you⁺ say, ‘We have found wisdom; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:13">let God drive him away, not man.’ <verse eid="JOB 32:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 32:14"/>And he has not arrayed <char style="add">his</char> words toward me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:14">and I will not answer him with your⁺ words. <verse eid="JOB 32:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 32:15"/>They are dismayed, <char style="add">and</char> do not answer anymore; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:15">the words have gone away from them. <verse eid="JOB 32:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 32:16"/>And I have waited, because they do not speak, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:16">because they stand there <char style="add">and</char> do not answer anymore? <verse eid="JOB 32:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 32:17"/>I will answer—even I—my portion; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:17">I will show my knowledge—even I. <verse eid="JOB 32:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 32:18"/>For I am full of words; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:18">the spirit <char style="add">in</char> my belly presses me. <verse eid="JOB 32:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 32:19"/>Behold, my belly <char style="add">is</char> like wine not opened; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:19">like new wineskins, it is bursting open. <verse eid="JOB 32:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 32:20"/>I will speak, and there is refreshment for me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:20">I will open my lips and answer. <verse eid="JOB 32:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 32:21"/>Do not, please, let me lift up the face of a man; and do not </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:21">let me give a title to man. <verse eid="JOB 32:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 32:22"/>For I do not know how to give a title; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 32:22">soon my Maker would take me away. <verse eid="JOB 32:22"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 32"/>

<chapter number="33" style="c" sid="JOB 33"/>

<para style="s">Elihu Rebukes Job</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 33:1"/><char style="add">“</char> But, please, O Job, hear my speech, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:1">and give ear <char style="add">to</char> all my words. <verse eid="JOB 33:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 33:2"/>Behold now, I open my mouth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:2">my tongue speaks in my palate. <verse eid="JOB 33:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 33:3"/>From the straightness of my heart <char style="add">are</char> my words, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:3">and my lips, being pure, speak knowledge. <verse eid="JOB 33:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 33:4"/>The Spirit of God has made me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:4">and the breath of Shaddai<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">33.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char></note> gives me life. <verse eid="JOB 33:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 33:5"/>If you are able to refute me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:5">arrange it before my face; station yourself. <verse eid="JOB 33:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 33:6"/>Behold, I <char style="add">am</char> according to your mouth before God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:6">from clay I also have been formed. <verse eid="JOB 33:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 33:7"/>Behold, my terror should not frighten you; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:7">and my hand on you shall not be heavy. <verse eid="JOB 33:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 33:8"/>Surely you have spoken in my ears, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:8">and the sound of the words I have heard. <verse eid="JOB 33:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 33:9"/>‘I <char style="add">am</char> pure, without transgression; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:9">I <char style="add">am</char> clean, and no iniquity <char style="add">is</char> in me. <verse eid="JOB 33:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 33:10"/>Behold, He finds occasions against me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:10">He reckons me as an enemy to Him. <verse eid="JOB 33:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 33:11"/>He puts my feet into the shackles; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:11">He watches all my paths.’ <verse eid="JOB 33:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 33:12"/>Behold, <char style="add">in</char> this you are not right; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:12">I will answer you, for God is greater than man. <verse eid="JOB 33:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 33:13"/>Why do you contend against Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:13">for all words He does not answer?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">33.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">that He answers for none of His actions</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 33:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 33:14"/>For once God speaks, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:14">and twice—one does not perceive it. <verse eid="JOB 33:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 33:15"/>In a dream, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:15">a vision of the night, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 33:15">in the falling of deep sleep upon men, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:15">in slumbers upon a bed, <verse eid="JOB 33:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 33:16"/>then He uncovers the ear of men, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:16">and with correction He seals <char style="add">them</char>, <verse eid="JOB 33:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 33:17"/>to turn aside a man from his doing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:17">and to conceal pride from a man. <verse eid="JOB 33:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 33:18"/>He holds back his soul from the Pit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:18">and his life from crossing over by a weapon. <verse eid="JOB 33:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 33:19"/>And he is churried with pain on his bed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:19">and strife in his bones is continual, <verse eid="JOB 33:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 33:20"/>and his life abhors bread, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:20">and his soul food of desire. <verse eid="JOB 33:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 33:21"/>His flesh is consumed from sight, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:21">and his bones <char style="add">that</char> were not seen are laid bare. <verse eid="JOB 33:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 33:22"/>And his soul draws near to the pit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:22">and his life to those causing death. <verse eid="JOB 33:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 33:23"/>If there is a messenger for him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:23">a mediator, one among a thousand, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 33:23">to declare to man his uprightness, <verse eid="JOB 33:23"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 33:24"/>and shows him favor and says, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 33:24">‘Spare him from going down <char style="add">into</char> the Pit; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:24">I have found a ransom,’ <verse eid="JOB 33:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 33:25"/><char style="add">then</char> his flesh is refreshed like a child’s, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:25"><char style="add">and</char> he returns to the days of his youth. <verse eid="JOB 33:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 33:26"/>He prays to God, and He shows him favor; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:26">and he sees His face with a shout of joy, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 33:26">and He restores to the man </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:26">His righteousness. <verse eid="JOB 33:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 33:27"/>Then he shall sing before men<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">33.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Then he looks upon men</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:27">and say, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 33:27">‘I have sinned, and have twisted uprightness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:27">and He did not requite <char style="add">it</char> of me. <verse eid="JOB 33:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 33:28"/>He has ransomed my soul from going down to the Pit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:28">and my life shall look on the light.’ <verse eid="JOB 33:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JOB 33:29"/>Behold, all these <char style="add">things</char> God does </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:29">two or three <char style="add">times</char> with a man, <verse eid="JOB 33:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JOB 33:30"/>to bring back his soul from the Pit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:30">to be enlightened with the light of the living. <verse eid="JOB 33:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JOB 33:31"/>Pay attention, O Job; listen to me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:31">be silent, and I will speak. <verse eid="JOB 33:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="JOB 33:32"/>If there are words, answer me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:32">speak, for I delight to prove you right. <verse eid="JOB 33:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="JOB 33:33"/>If not, <char style="add">then</char> you must listen to me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 33:33">keep silent, and I will teach you wisdom.” <verse eid="JOB 33:33"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 33"/>

<chapter number="34" style="c" sid="JOB 34"/>

<para style="s">Elihu Confirms God’s Justice</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 34:1"/>And Elihu answered and said, <verse eid="JOB 34:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 34:2"/>“Hear, O wise men, my words, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:2">and give ear to me, knowing ones. <verse eid="JOB 34:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 34:3"/>For the ear shall test words, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:3">and the palate tastes to eat. <verse eid="JOB 34:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 34:4"/>Let us choose for ourselves what is just; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:4">let us know among ourselves what <char style="add">is</char> good. <verse eid="JOB 34:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 34:5"/>For Job has said, ‘I am righteous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:5">and God has turned aside my justice. <verse eid="JOB 34:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 34:6"/><char style="add">And</char> over my justice should I lie? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:6">Mortal <char style="add">is</char> my arrow, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:6">without transgression.’ <verse eid="JOB 34:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 34:7"/>Who <char style="add">is</char> a man like Job, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:7">drinking up derision like the water, <verse eid="JOB 34:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 34:8"/>and he travels in company with workers of iniquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:8">and in walking with men of wickedness? <verse eid="JOB 34:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 34:9"/>For he has said, ‘Nothing does it profit a man </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:9">that he should delight in God.’ <verse eid="JOB 34:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 34:10"/>Therefore, O men of heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:10">listen to me. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 34:10">Far be it to God from wickedness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:10">and Shaddai from injustice. <verse eid="JOB 34:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 34:11"/>For the work of man, he repays to him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:11">and according to the way of a man, He causes him to find <char style="add">it</char>. <verse eid="JOB 34:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 34:12"/>Yes, surely God does not act wickedly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:12">and Shaddai does not pervert justice. <verse eid="JOB 34:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 34:13"/>Who gave charge to Him over the earth? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:13">And who has set <char style="add">Him</char> <char style="add">over</char> all of the world? <verse eid="JOB 34:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 34:14"/>If He should set His heart to it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:14">gathering His Spirit and His breath to Himself, <verse eid="JOB 34:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 34:15"/><char style="add">then</char> all flesh would perish together, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:15">and man would return to the dust. <verse eid="JOB 34:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 34:16"/>And if <char style="add">there is</char> understanding, hear this; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:16">give ear to the sound of my words. <verse eid="JOB 34:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 34:17"/>And shall one hating justice govern? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:17">Or will you declare wicked the just and mighty One? <verse eid="JOB 34:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 34:18"/>Who says to a king, ‘Worthless,’ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:18"><char style="add">or</char> to nobles, ‘Wicked’? <verse eid="JOB 34:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 34:19"/>Who does not lift the faces of princes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:19">and does not acknowledge the rich before the face of the poor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:19">for they <char style="add">are</char> all the work of His hands. <verse eid="JOB 34:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 34:20"/><char style="add">In</char> a moment they die, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:20">and in the middle of the night </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 34:20">the people are shaken and pass away; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:20">and the mighty are taken away, not by a hand. <verse eid="JOB 34:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 34:21"/>For His eyes <char style="add">are</char> upon the ways of man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:21">and all of his steps He sees. <verse eid="JOB 34:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 34:22"/>There is no darkness and no shadow of death, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:22"><char style="add">for</char> the workers of iniquity to be hidden there. <verse eid="JOB 34:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 34:23"/>For He does not set upon a man further, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:23">for his going before God in the judgment. <verse eid="JOB 34:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 34:24"/>He breaks the mighty without investigation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:24">and makes others stand in their place. <verse eid="JOB 34:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 34:25"/>Therefore, He recognizes their works, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:25">and He overturns <char style="add">them</char> in the night, and they are crushed. <verse eid="JOB 34:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 34:26"/>In exchange for their wickednesses, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:26">He strikes them in a place of seeing, <verse eid="JOB 34:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 34:27"/>which <char style="add">was</char> upon thus: They turned aside from Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:27">and they had no regard for any of His ways, <verse eid="JOB 34:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 34:28"/>They caused the cry of the poor to cause to come before Him—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:28">and He heard the cry of the afflicted. <verse eid="JOB 34:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JOB 34:29"/>And he is silent, and who can call Him wicked? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:29">And He hides <char style="add">His</char> face, and who can see Him? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 34:29">And He is over a nation and over man alike, <verse eid="JOB 34:29"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JOB 34:30"/>from the reigning of godless a man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:30">from the snares of the people. <verse eid="JOB 34:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JOB 34:31"/>If one says to God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:31">‘I have lifted <char style="add">it</char>, <char style="add">and</char> no more will I offend; <verse eid="JOB 34:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="JOB 34:32"/>besides what I see, You teach me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:32">if I have done iniquity, I will not continue <char style="add">it</char>’ <verse eid="JOB 34:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="JOB 34:33"/>will he repay it from with you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:33">because you have rejected <char style="add">it</char>? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 34:33">Then you must choose, and not I, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:33">and may you speak what you know. <verse eid="JOB 34:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="JOB 34:34"/>Men of understanding will say to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:34">and the wise man <char style="add">who is</char> listening to me: <verse eid="JOB 34:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="JOB 34:35"/>‘Job <char style="add">does</char> not speak with knowledge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:35">and His words <char style="add">are</char> not with wisdom.’ <verse eid="JOB 34:35"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="JOB 34:36"/>If only Job were tested to the end, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:36">upon his answers among men of iniquity! <verse eid="JOB 34:36"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="JOB 34:37"/>For he adds rebellion upon his sin; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:37">among us he claps, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 34:37">and he multiplies his words against God.” </para>

<para style="p" vid="JOB 34:37"> <char style="add">Shaddai</char> means <char style="add">the Almighty</char>; also in verse 12<verse eid="JOB 34:37"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 34"/>

<chapter number="35" style="c" sid="JOB 35"/>

<para style="s">Elihu Recalls God’s Justice</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 35:1"/>And Elihu answered and said: <verse eid="JOB 35:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 35:2"/>“This do you reckon to be justice? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 35:2">You say, ‘I am righteous above God.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">35.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">‘I am righteous before God.’</char></note>’ <verse eid="JOB 35:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 35:3"/>Indeed you say, ‘What does it benefit You? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 35:3">What do I gain from my sin?” <verse eid="JOB 35:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 35:4"/>I will return to you the words, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 35:4">and <char style="add">to</char> your friends with you. <verse eid="JOB 35:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 35:5"/>Look to the heavens and see, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 35:5">and behold the clouds—they are higher than you. <verse eid="JOB 35:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 35:6"/>If you have sinned, what do you accomplish against Him? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 35:6">Or <char style="add">if</char> your transgressions are multiplied, what do you do to Him? <verse eid="JOB 35:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 35:7"/>If you are righteous, what do you give to Him? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 35:7">Or what does He receive from your hand? <verse eid="JOB 35:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 35:8"/>Your wickedness <char style="add">is</char> to a man such as you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 35:8">and your righteousness to a son of man. <verse eid="JOB 35:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 35:9"/>From the multitude of oppressions they cry out; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 35:9">they cry for help from the arm of the mighty. <verse eid="JOB 35:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 35:10"/>Yet no one says, ‘Where <char style="add">is</char> God my Maker, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 35:10">the One giving songs in the night, <verse eid="JOB 35:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 35:11"/>teaching us more than the beasts of the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 35:11">and making us wiser than the birds of the heavens?’ <verse eid="JOB 35:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 35:12"/>There they cry out, but He does not answer, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 35:12">from the face of the pride of evil ones. <verse eid="JOB 35:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 35:13"/>Surely God will not listen <char style="add">to</char> vanity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 35:13">and Shaddai<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">35.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char></note> will not regard it. <verse eid="JOB 35:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 35:14"/>Indeed, though you say <char style="add">that</char> you do not see Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 35:14">justice <char style="add">is</char> before His face, and you must wait for Him. <verse eid="JOB 35:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 35:15"/>And now, because He does not visit His anger, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 35:15">and has not taken much note of transgression, <verse eid="JOB 35:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 35:16"/>and Job opens his mouth in vain; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 35:16">he multiplies words without knowledge.” <verse eid="JOB 35:16"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 35"/>

<chapter number="36" style="c" sid="JOB 36"/>

<para style="s">Elihu Describes God’s Power</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 36:1"/>And Elihu added and said: <verse eid="JOB 36:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 36:2"/>“Surround unto me a little, and I will show you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:2">that <char style="add">there are</char> words yet to God. <verse eid="JOB 36:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 36:3"/>I will lift up my knowledge from afar, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:3">and to my Maker I will ascribe righteousness. <verse eid="JOB 36:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 36:4"/>For truly, my words <char style="add">are</char> not false; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:4">the one complete in knowledge <char style="add">is</char> with you. <verse eid="JOB 36:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 36:5"/>Behold, God <char style="add">is</char> mighty, and He does not despise; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:5"><char style="add">He is</char> mighty <char style="add">in</char> strength of heart. <verse eid="JOB 36:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 36:6"/>He does not keep the wicked alive, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:6">and He gives justice to the afflicted. <verse eid="JOB 36:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 36:7"/>He does not take away His eyes from the righteous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:7">but <char style="add">they are</char> with kings on the throne; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:7">and He has seated them forever, and they are exalted. <verse eid="JOB 36:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 36:8"/>And if they are bound in the fetters, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:8">caught in the cords of affliction, <verse eid="JOB 36:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 36:9"/>then he declares to them their work and their transgressions, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:9">because they magnified themselves. <verse eid="JOB 36:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 36:10"/>And He opens their ear to correction, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:10">and He says that they should turn back from iniquity. <verse eid="JOB 36:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 36:11"/>If they do hear and serve, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:11">they will complete their days in good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:11">and their years in pleasantness. <verse eid="JOB 36:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 36:12"/>And if they do not obey, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:12">by a weapon they shall pass away,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">36.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the river of death they shall cross</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:12">and they shall die as without knowledge. <verse eid="JOB 36:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 36:13"/>And the godless of heart set the nose; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:13">they do not cry out when He binds them. <verse eid="JOB 36:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 36:14"/>Their soul dies in youth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:14">and their life among the male shrine prostitutes. <verse eid="JOB 36:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 36:15"/>He rescues the afflicted one by his affliction, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:15">and uncovers their ear by oppression. <verse eid="JOB 36:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 36:16"/>And indeed He has drawn you from the mouth of distress, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:16"><char style="add">into</char> a broad place without constraint under it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:16">and the resting of your table is full of richness. <verse eid="JOB 36:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 36:17"/>And you are filled <char style="add">with</char> the judgment of the wicked; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:17">judgment and justice take hold— <verse eid="JOB 36:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 36:18"/>for wrath, lest it entice you with mocking, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:18">and a large bribe not let it stretch you. <verse eid="JOB 36:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 36:19"/>Can your opulence<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">36.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">your cry for help</char></note> make arrangement in time of distress, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:19">or all the forces of strength? <verse eid="JOB 36:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 36:20"/>Do not long for the night, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:20">for the coming up of peoples in place of them. <verse eid="JOB 36:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 36:21"/>Take heed not to turn to iniquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:21">for upon this you have been chosen by affliction. <verse eid="JOB 36:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 36:22"/>Behold, God is exalted in His power; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:22">who <char style="add">is</char> a teacher like Him? <verse eid="JOB 36:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 36:23"/>Who has appointed for Him His way? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:23">Or who has said, ‘You have done unrighteousness’? <verse eid="JOB 36:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 36:24"/>Remember that you should magnify His work, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:24">of which men have sung. <verse eid="JOB 36:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 36:25"/>Every man has gazed on it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:25">mankind looks on <char style="add">it</char> from afar. <verse eid="JOB 36:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 36:26"/>Behold, God <char style="add">is</char> great, and we do not know <char style="add">Him</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:26">and <char style="add">there is</char> no searching the number of His years. <verse eid="JOB 36:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 36:27"/>For He draws up drops of water; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:27">they distill as rain from the mist, <verse eid="JOB 36:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 36:28"/>which the clouds pour down; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:28">they drop upon man in abundance. <verse eid="JOB 36:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JOB 36:29"/>Indeed, if one will understand the spreading out of a cloud, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:29">the noises <char style="add">from</char> His pavilion? <verse eid="JOB 36:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JOB 36:30"/>Behold, He scatters His lightning around Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:30">and covers the depths of the sea. <verse eid="JOB 36:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JOB 36:31"/>For by these He judges<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">36.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">governs</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">nourishes</char></note> the peoples; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:31">He gives food in abundance. <verse eid="JOB 36:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="JOB 36:32"/>With <char style="add">His</char> palms He covers the lightning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:32">and He gives a charge upon it for <char style="add">its</char> striking. <verse eid="JOB 36:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="JOB 36:33"/><char style="add">By</char> its shouting He declares concerning it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 36:33">the cattle also concerning the arising. <verse eid="JOB 36:33"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 36"/>

<chapter number="37" style="c" sid="JOB 37"/>

<para style="s">Elihu Proclaims God’s Majesty</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 37:1"/><char style="add">“</char> Indeed at this my heart trembles, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:1">and it leaps from its place. <verse eid="JOB 37:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 37:2"/>Listen closely to the quaking of His voice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:2">and the rumbling from His mouth <char style="add">that</char> comes forth. <verse eid="JOB 37:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 37:3"/>Beneath all the heaven He unleashes it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:3">and His lightning <char style="add">is</char> over the edges of the earth. <verse eid="JOB 37:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 37:4"/>After it, a voice roars; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:4">He thunders with the voice of His majesty, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 37:4">and He does not restrain them </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:4">when His voice is heard. <verse eid="JOB 37:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 37:5"/>God thunders with His voice wondrously; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:5">He does great <char style="add">things</char> that we cannot know. <verse eid="JOB 37:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 37:6"/>For to the snow He says, ‘Fall <char style="add">on</char> the earth,’ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:6">and to the shower of rain, and to the shower, ‘<char style="add">Be</char> the rains of His might.’ <verse eid="JOB 37:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 37:7"/>He seals up the hand of every man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:7">for the knowing of His work <char style="add">by</char> all men. <verse eid="JOB 37:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 37:8"/>And the beast comes into <char style="add">its</char> lair, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:8">and in its dens it shall dwell. <verse eid="JOB 37:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 37:9"/>From <char style="add">its</char> chamber the whirlwind comes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:9">and the cold from the scattering winds. <verse eid="JOB 37:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 37:10"/>From the breath of God, ice is given, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:10">and the breadth of the waters <char style="add">is</char> in constraint. <verse eid="JOB 37:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 37:11"/>Also with moisture He loads the thick cloud; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:11">His lightning scatters the cloud. <verse eid="JOB 37:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 37:12"/>And it turns around, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:12">being turned <char style="add">about</char> by His guidance, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 37:12">to do all of what He commands them </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:12">above the face of the habitation of the earth. <verse eid="JOB 37:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 37:13"/>If for the rod, if for His land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:13">if in His loving devotion, He makes it find it. <verse eid="JOB 37:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 37:14"/>Give ear to this, O Job; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:14">stand and consider the wonders of God. <verse eid="JOB 37:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 37:15"/>Do you know <char style="add">how</char> God does place upon them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:15">and <char style="add">how</char> He causes the light of His cloud to shine? <verse eid="JOB 37:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 37:16"/>Do you know about the balancing of the cloud, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:16">the wonders of the One perfect in knowledge, <verse eid="JOB 37:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 37:17"/><char style="add">you</char> whose garments <char style="add">are</char> hot </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:17">in the quieting of the earth from the south? <verse eid="JOB 37:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 37:18"/>Have you beaten the skies with him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:18">strong as a mirror of cast metal? <verse eid="JOB 37:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 37:19"/>Make us know what we should say to Him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:19">we cannot arrange from the face of the darkness. <verse eid="JOB 37:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 37:20"/>Should it be told to Him that I would speak, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:20">If a man spoke that he would be swallowed up?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">37.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Would a man ask to be swallowed up?</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 37:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 37:21"/>And now they cannot look at the light; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:21">it <char style="add">is</char> bright in the clouds </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:21">when the wind has passed over and cleansed them. <verse eid="JOB 37:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 37:22"/>Gold comes from the north; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:22">upon God <char style="add">is</char> a fearsome majesty. <verse eid="JOB 37:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 37:23"/>Shaddai<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">37.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char></note>—we cannot find Him out! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:23"><char style="add">He is</char> great <char style="add">in</char> power and judgment, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 37:23">and abundant <char style="add">in</char> righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:23">He does not oppress. <verse eid="JOB 37:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 37:24"/>Therefore men fear Him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 37:24">He does not regard any of the wise of heart.” <verse eid="JOB 37:24"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 37"/>

<chapter number="38" style="c" sid="JOB 38"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Challenges Job</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 38:1"/>And YHWH answered Job out of the whirlwind, and He said: <verse eid="JOB 38:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 38:2"/>“Who <char style="add">is</char> this darkening counsel </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:2">with words lacking knowledge? <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">38.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Job 42:3</char></note><verse eid="JOB 38:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 38:3"/>Gird up your loins now like a man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:3">and I will question you, and you shall answer Me. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">38.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Job 42:4</char></note><verse eid="JOB 38:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 38:4"/>Where were you at my founding of the earth? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:4">Declare it if you know <char style="add">with</char> understanding. <verse eid="JOB 38:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 38:5"/>Who set its measurements? Surely you must know! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:5">Or who stretched over it a line? <verse eid="JOB 38:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 38:6"/>On what were its bases made to sink <char style="add">in</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:6">or who cast the stone of its corner,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">38.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">who set its core in place</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 38:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 38:7"/>at the singing together <char style="add">by</char> the stars of the morning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:7">and all the sons of God shouted for joy? <verse eid="JOB 38:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 38:8"/>Or <char style="add">who</char> shut in the sea with doors, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:8">at its coming forth in its bursting from the womb, <verse eid="JOB 38:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 38:9"/>in my setting <char style="add">for</char> the cloud its garment, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:9">and <char style="add">for</char> the dark cloud its swaddling band, <verse eid="JOB 38:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 38:10"/>when I broke forth over it My decree, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:10">and set in place a bar and doors, <verse eid="JOB 38:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 38:11"/>and I said, ‘Up to here you may come, and you shall not go further; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:11">and here shall be set the pride of your waves’? <verse eid="JOB 38:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 38:12"/>have you commanded the morning from your days, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:12"><char style="add">and</char> made the dawn to know its place, <verse eid="JOB 38:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 38:13"/>for <char style="add">it</char> to take hold of the edges of the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:13">and the wicked be shaken out of it? <verse eid="JOB 38:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 38:14"/>It is turned over like clay under a seal, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:14">and they stand out like a garment. <verse eid="JOB 38:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 38:15"/>And their light is withheld from the wicked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:15">and the arm upraised is broken. <verse eid="JOB 38:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 38:16"/>Have you come to the springs of the sea, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:16">or in search of the depths have you walked about? <verse eid="JOB 38:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 38:17"/>Have the gates of death been uncovered to you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:17">or have you seen the doors of the shadow of death? <verse eid="JOB 38:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 38:18"/>Have you comprehended to the breadths of the earth? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:18">Declare it if you know all of it. <verse eid="JOB 38:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 38:19"/>Where <char style="add">is</char> this way <char style="add">to</char> the dwelling of light? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:19">And of darkness, where <char style="add">is</char> this its place, <verse eid="JOB 38:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 38:20"/>that you may take it to its border, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:20">that you may know the paths <char style="add">to</char> its home? <verse eid="JOB 38:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 38:21"/>You must know <char style="add">it</char>, for you were born then, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:21">and the number of your days <char style="add">is</char> great! <verse eid="JOB 38:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 38:22"/>Have you come to the treasury of snow, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:22">or have you seen the treasury of hail, <verse eid="JOB 38:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 38:23"/>that I have held back for a time of trouble, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:23">for a day of battle and war? <verse eid="JOB 38:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 38:24"/>Where <char style="add">is</char> this, the way light is apportioned? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:24">The east wind is scattered over the earth. <verse eid="JOB 38:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 38:25"/>Who has divided out a channel for the flood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:25">or a path for the lightning of the thunderings, <verse eid="JOB 38:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 38:26"/>to make rain come upon a land without man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:26">a desert without man in it, <verse eid="JOB 38:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 38:27"/>to satisfy the waste and the desolation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:27">and to make sprout the shoot of the grass? <verse eid="JOB 38:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 38:28"/>Is there a father for the rain? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:28">Or who has begotten the drops of dew? <verse eid="JOB 38:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JOB 38:29"/>From whose womb comes forth the ice? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:29">And the frost of the heavens, who gives birth to it? <verse eid="JOB 38:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JOB 38:30"/>Like stone, the waters hide themselves, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:30">and the face of the deep is seized. <verse eid="JOB 38:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JOB 38:31"/>Can you bind the chains of the Pleiades, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:31">or can you open the cords of Orion? <verse eid="JOB 38:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="JOB 38:32"/>Can you bring forth Mazzaroth in its time?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">38.32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Can you bring forth the constellations in their seasons</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:32">Or can you lead out the Bear<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">38.32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Leo</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Arcturus</char></note> with her cubs? <verse eid="JOB 38:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="JOB 38:33"/>Do you know the ordinances of the heavens? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:33">Or can you set its rule over the earth? <verse eid="JOB 38:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="JOB 38:34"/>Can you raise to the cloud your voice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:34">and an abundance of waters will cover you? <verse eid="JOB 38:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="JOB 38:35"/>Can you send out lightnings, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:35">that they may go and say to you, ‘Behold us’? <verse eid="JOB 38:35"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="JOB 38:36"/>Who has put wisdom in the inner parts?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">38.36 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Who has given the ibis wisdom</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, that is, wisdom about the flooding of the Nile</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:36">Or who has given to the heart understanding? <verse eid="JOB 38:36"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="JOB 38:37"/>Who can count the clouds by wisdom? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:37">Or the water skins of the heavens, who can tilt, <verse eid="JOB 38:37"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="JOB 38:38"/>in the pouring of the dust into a mass, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:38">and the clods clinging together? <verse eid="JOB 38:38"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="JOB 38:39"/>Can you hunt prey for a lion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:39">or satisfy the life of young lions, <verse eid="JOB 38:39"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="JOB 38:40"/>when they crouch in the dens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:40">dwelling in a thicket, lying in wait in <char style="add">it</char>? <verse eid="JOB 38:40"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="JOB 38:41"/>Who provides to the raven its food </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:41">when its children cry out to God </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 38:41">and wander for lack of food? <verse eid="JOB 38:41"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 38"/>

<chapter number="39" style="c" sid="JOB 39"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Speaks of His Creation</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 39:1"/><char style="add">“</char> Do you know the time of the bearing of the goats of the rock? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:1">Can you observe the twisting of the does? <verse eid="JOB 39:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 39:2"/>Can you number the months they fulfill? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:2">Or do you know the time of their giving birth? <verse eid="JOB 39:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 39:3"/>They bend down <char style="add">and</char> squeeze out their young; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:3">their labor pains they send forth. <verse eid="JOB 39:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 39:4"/>Their young ones are healthy; they increase in the field; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:4">they go forth and do not return to them. <verse eid="JOB 39:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 39:5"/>Who sent away the wild donkey free? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:5">And who opened the bonds of the swift donkey, <verse eid="JOB 39:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 39:6"/>whose I have made the Arabah house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:6">the salt land <char style="add">as</char> his dwelling? <verse eid="JOB 39:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 39:7"/>He laughs at the tumult of the city; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:7">the shouts of the driver he does not hear. <verse eid="JOB 39:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 39:8"/>He searches out the mountains for his pasture, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:8">and after every green thing he searches. <verse eid="JOB 39:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 39:9"/>Is the wild ox willing to serve you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:9">or will he lodge by your manger? <verse eid="JOB 39:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 39:10"/>Can you bind the wild ox in the furrow with a cord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:10">or will he harrow the valleys after you? <verse eid="JOB 39:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 39:11"/>Will you trust in him because his strength <char style="add">is</char> great, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:11">and will you leave to him your labor? <verse eid="JOB 39:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 39:12"/>Will you trust in him that he will bring back your grain </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:12">and gather <char style="add">it</char> <char style="add">to</char> your threshing floor? <verse eid="JOB 39:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 39:13"/>The wings of the ostrich rejoice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:13">but <char style="add">are</char> not the pinions<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">39.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Pinions</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> are the outer parts of a bird’s wings, including the flight feathers.</char></note> of a stork and its feathers. <verse eid="JOB 39:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 39:14"/>For she leaves her eggs on the ground, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:14">and upon the dust she warms <char style="add">them</char>, <verse eid="JOB 39:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 39:15"/>and she forgets that a foot may crush it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:15">or that a creature of the field might tread <char style="add">over</char> it. <verse eid="JOB 39:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 39:16"/>Her young she treats harshly as though not unto her; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:16">her labor <char style="add">is</char> in vain, without dread; <verse eid="JOB 39:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 39:17"/>for God made her forget wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:17">and He has not given a portion to her in understanding. <verse eid="JOB 39:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 39:18"/>At the time she lifts herself up on high, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:18">she laughs at the horse and at its rider. <verse eid="JOB 39:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 39:19"/>Have you given the horse strength? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:19">Did you clothe his neck with a mane? <verse eid="JOB 39:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 39:20"/>Can you cause him to rush like a locust? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:20">The majesty of his snorting <char style="add">is</char> terror. <verse eid="JOB 39:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 39:21"/>They dig in the valley, and he rejoices in strength; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:21">he goes forth to meet the weaponry. <verse eid="JOB 39:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 39:22"/>He laughs at dread and is not dismayed; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:22">he does not turn back from the face of the sword. <verse eid="JOB 39:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 39:23"/>Upon him rattles the quiver, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:23">the flame of the spear and lance.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">39.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">javelin</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 39:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 39:24"/>With quaking and raging he swallows the ground; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:24">he cannot stand still because of the voice of the shofar. <verse eid="JOB 39:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 39:25"/>In the abundance of the shofar, he says, ‘Aha!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">39.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">he snorts with fervor</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char></note>’ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:25">And from afar He smells the battle, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:25">the thunder of captains and shouting. <verse eid="JOB 39:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 39:26"/>By your understanding does the hawk soar </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:26"><char style="add">and</char> spread his wings toward the south? <verse eid="JOB 39:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 39:27"/><char style="add">Is it</char> by your mouth <char style="add">that</char> the eagle mounts up </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:27">and makes his nest on high? <verse eid="JOB 39:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 39:28"/><char style="add">In</char> the rock he dwells and lodges </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:28">and his stronghold <char style="add">is</char> upon the tooth of the rock. <verse eid="JOB 39:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JOB 39:29"/>From there he searches out food; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:29">from afar his eyes observe. <verse eid="JOB 39:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JOB 39:30"/>And his young ones suck up blood; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 39:30">and where the slain <char style="add">are</char>, there he <char style="add">is</char>.” <verse eid="JOB 39:30"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 39"/>

<chapter number="40" style="c" sid="JOB 40"/>

<para style="s">Job Humbles Himself before Yahweh</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 40:1"/>And YHWH answered Job and said, <verse eid="JOB 40:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 40:2"/>“Is a reprover to contend with Shaddai?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:2">One rebuking God, let him answer it.” <verse eid="JOB 40:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 40:3"/>And Job answered YHWH and said, <verse eid="JOB 40:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 40:4"/>“Behold, I am slight. How can I reply to You? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:4">My hand I place over my mouth. <verse eid="JOB 40:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 40:5"/>Once I have spoken, and I will not answer—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:5">and twice, and I will not add.” <verse eid="JOB 40:5"/></para>

<para style="s">Yahweh Challenges Job Again</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 40:6"/>And YHWH answered Job from the whirlwind, and He said, <verse eid="JOB 40:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 40:7"/>“Gird up now your loins like a man; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:7">I will question you, and you shall let Me know. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Job 42:4</char></note><verse eid="JOB 40:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 40:8"/>Would you even break My judgment? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:8">Would you consider Me wicked so that you may be proved right? <verse eid="JOB 40:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 40:9"/>Is there an arm like God’s unto you? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:9">Or with a voice like His can you thunder? <verse eid="JOB 40:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 40:10"/>Adorn yourself, please, <char style="add">with</char> majesty and loftiness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:10">and with honor and glory clothe yourself. <verse eid="JOB 40:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 40:11"/>Scatter the fury of your nose, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:11">and look on every proud one, and bring him low. <verse eid="JOB 40:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 40:12"/>Look on every proud one, and humble him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:12">and tread down the wicked in their place. <verse eid="JOB 40:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 40:13"/>Hide them in the dust together; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:13">bind their faces in the hidden place.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the grave</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 40:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 40:14"/>And then I will confess to you </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:14">that your right hand can bring salvation to you. <verse eid="JOB 40:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 40:15"/>Behold, please, Behemoth, which I made with you; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:15">he eats grass like the ox. <verse eid="JOB 40:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 40:16"/>Behold, please, his strength <char style="add">is</char> in his loins, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:16">and his power <char style="add">is</char> in the muscles of his belly. <verse eid="JOB 40:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 40:17"/>He bends his tail like a cedar; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:17">the sinews of his thighs are tightly knit. <verse eid="JOB 40:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 40:18"/>His bones <char style="add">are</char> tubes of bronze; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:18">his limbs are like bars of iron. <verse eid="JOB 40:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 40:19"/>He <char style="add">is</char> the first of the ways<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">works</char></note> of God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:19">his Maker can bring near His sword. <verse eid="JOB 40:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 40:20"/>For the mountains carry produce to him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:20">and all the creatures of the field play there. <verse eid="JOB 40:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 40:21"/>Beneath the lotus trees<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">bramble bushes</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 22</char></note> he lies down, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:21">in the covering of reed and marsh. <verse eid="JOB 40:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 40:22"/>The lotus trees cover him <char style="add">with</char> their shade; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:22">the willows<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">poplars</char></note> of the brook surround him. <verse eid="JOB 40:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 40:23"/>Though the river may press, he does not hurry <char style="add">off</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:23">he is secure, though the Jordan should burst forth toward his mouth. <verse eid="JOB 40:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 40:24"/>Can one take him by his eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 40:24"><char style="add">or</char> pierce <char style="add">his</char> nose with snares? <verse eid="JOB 40:24"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 40"/>

<chapter number="41" style="c" sid="JOB 41"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh’s Power Shown in Leviathan</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 41:1"/><char style="add">“</char> Can you draw out Leviathan with a hook, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:1">and press down his tongue with a rope? <verse eid="JOB 41:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 41:2"/>Can you put a cord in his nose, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:2">and with a hook pierce his jaw? <verse eid="JOB 41:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 41:3"/>Will he multiply to you supplications? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:3">Indeed, will he speak to you softly? <verse eid="JOB 41:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 41:4"/>Will he cut a covenant with you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:4">to take him as a slave forever? <verse eid="JOB 41:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 41:5"/>Will you play with him like a bird, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:5">and leash him for your maidens? <verse eid="JOB 41:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 41:6"/>Will traders barter for him? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:6">Will they divide him among the merchants? <verse eid="JOB 41:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 41:7"/>Can you fill his skin with harpoons, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:7">or his head with spears of fishing? <verse eid="JOB 41:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 41:8"/>Put your hands on him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:8">may you remember the battle, <char style="add">and</char> not add. <verse eid="JOB 41:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 41:9"/>Behold, the hope of him is false. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:9"><char style="add">One is</char> even cast down at the sight of him. <verse eid="JOB 41:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 41:10"/>None <char style="add">is</char> so fierce that he would rouse him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:10">and who is he who will stand before my face? <verse eid="JOB 41:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 41:11"/>Who has brought before Me that I should repay <char style="add">him</char>? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:11">Under all the heavens it <char style="add">is</char> unto Me. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Romans 11:35</char></note><verse eid="JOB 41:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 41:12"/>I will not keep silent about his limbs, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:12">and the matter of his strength and the grace of his form. <verse eid="JOB 41:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 41:13"/>Who can uncover the face of his clothing? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:13">Who can enter into the double of his bridle?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Who can come within his double mail?</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 41:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 41:14"/>The doors of his face, who can open <char style="add">them</char>? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:14">All around his teeth <char style="add">are</char> terror. <verse eid="JOB 41:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 41:15"/><char style="add">His</char> rows of shields are <char style="add">his</char> pride, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:15">shut up tight with a seal. <verse eid="JOB 41:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 41:16"/>One by one they draw near, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:16">and air cannot come between them. <verse eid="JOB 41:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 41:17"/>They are joined a man to his brother; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:17">they clasp together and cannot be separated. <verse eid="JOB 41:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JOB 41:18"/>His sneezings flash forth light, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:18">and his eyes <char style="add">are</char> like the eyelids of the dawn. <verse eid="JOB 41:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JOB 41:19"/>From his mouth torches go forth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:19">sparks of fire leap out. <verse eid="JOB 41:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JOB 41:20"/>From his nostrils smoke comes forth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:20">boiling like a pot and a reed. <verse eid="JOB 41:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JOB 41:21"/>His breath will kindle the coals, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:21">and a flame goes forth from his mouth. <verse eid="JOB 41:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JOB 41:22"/>In his neck lodges strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:22">and before him terror dances. <verse eid="JOB 41:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JOB 41:23"/>The folds of his flesh are joined together, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:23">c on him, <char style="add">and</char> it annot be shaken. <verse eid="JOB 41:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JOB 41:24"/>His heart is as firm as a stone, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:24">even as firm as a lower millstone. <verse eid="JOB 41:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JOB 41:25"/>From his rising up the mighty are afraid; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:25">before his thrashing they cleanse themselves from sin. <verse eid="JOB 41:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JOB 41:26"/>The sword reaching him shall not stand—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:26"><char style="add">not</char> spear, dart, or lance. <verse eid="JOB 41:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JOB 41:27"/>He regards iron as straw, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:27"><char style="add">and</char> bronze as rotten wood. <verse eid="JOB 41:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="JOB 41:28"/>The son of the bow cannot make him flee; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:28">the stones of the sling are turned over before him like stubble. <verse eid="JOB 41:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="JOB 41:29"/>A club is regarded as stubble, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:29">and he laughs at the rattle of a lance.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">javelin</char></note> <verse eid="JOB 41:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="JOB 41:30"/>Beneath him are points of a shard; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:30">he spreads out like a threshing sledge upon the mud. <verse eid="JOB 41:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="JOB 41:31"/>He makes the deep boil like a pot; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:31">he makes the sea like an ointment pot. <verse eid="JOB 41:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="JOB 41:32"/>Behind him he makes a path shine; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:32">one would think the deep <char style="add">were</char> white-haired. <verse eid="JOB 41:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="JOB 41:33"/>There is nothing on earth like him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:33">the one made devoid of fear. <verse eid="JOB 41:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="JOB 41:34"/>He beholds every high <char style="add">thing</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 41:34">he <char style="add">is</char> king over all the sons of pride.” <verse eid="JOB 41:34"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 41"/>

<chapter number="42" style="c" sid="JOB 42"/>

<para style="s">Job Submits Himself to Yahweh</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="JOB 42:1"/>And Job answered YHWH and said: <verse eid="JOB 42:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JOB 42:2"/>“I know that You are able <char style="add">to do</char> all things, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 42:2">and a plan from You cannot be thwarted. <verse eid="JOB 42:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JOB 42:3"/>‘Who <char style="add">is</char> this, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 42:3">concealing counsel without knowledge?’ </para>

<para style="q1" vid="JOB 42:3">So I have declared, and did not understand—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 42:3">things too wonderful for me, and I did not know. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">42.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Job 38:2</char></note><verse eid="JOB 42:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JOB 42:4"/>‘Listen now, and I will speak. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 42:4">I will question you, and you shall inform Me.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">42.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Job 38:3 and Job 40:7</char></note><verse eid="JOB 42:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JOB 42:5"/>By the hearing of the ear I had heard of You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 42:5">and now my eye has seen You. <verse eid="JOB 42:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JOB 42:6"/>Upon thus I despise <char style="add">it</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="JOB 42:6">and I repent in dust and ashes.” <verse eid="JOB 42:6"/></para>

<para style="s">Yahweh Rebukes Job’s Friends</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JOB 42:7"/>And it came to pass, after YHWH had spoken these words to Job, that YHWH said to Eliphaz the Temanite, “My anger is kindled against you, and against the two friends of yours, for you have⁺ not spoken of Me accurately as My servant Job <char style="add">has</char>. <verse eid="JOB 42:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JOB 42:8"/>And now, take for yourselves seven bulls and seven rams, and go to My servant Job, and offer up a burnt offering for yourselves. And Job My servant shall pray for you⁺ (for surely I will lift his face), so as not to deal with your⁺ folly, for you⁺ have not spoken of Me accurately, as My servant Job <char style="add">has</char>.” <verse eid="JOB 42:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JOB 42:9"/>Eliphaz the Temanite, and Bildad the Shuhite, <char style="add">and</char> Zophar the Naamathite went and did according to what YHWH had spoken to them; and YHWH lifted up the face of Job. <verse eid="JOB 42:9"/></para>

<para style="s">Yahweh Blesses Job</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JOB 42:10"/>And YHWH turned back the captivity of Job, in his praying for his friends; and YHWH added <char style="add">to</char> all that <char style="add">was</char> unto Job—to double. <verse eid="JOB 42:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JOB 42:11"/>All his brothers, and all his sisters, and all the faces of those knowing him came to him, and they ate bread with him in his house, and they nodded to him and comforted him over all the adversity that YHWH had brought upon him. And each man gave to him one kesitah,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">42.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">one piece of silver</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; the value or weight of the kesitah is no longer known.</char></note> and each man one ring of gold. <verse eid="JOB 42:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JOB 42:12"/>And YHWH blessed the latter of Job more than his first, and there were unto him fourteen thousand sheep, and six thousand camels, and a thousand yoke of oxen, and a thousand female donkeys. <verse eid="JOB 42:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JOB 42:13"/>And there were unto him seven sons and three daughters. <verse eid="JOB 42:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JOB 42:14"/>And he called the name of the first Jemimah, and the name of the second Keziah, and the name of the third Keren-happuch. <verse eid="JOB 42:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JOB 42:15"/>And there were not found women <char style="add">as</char> beautiful as the daughters of Job in all the land; and their father gave to them an inheritance in the midst of their brothers. <verse eid="JOB 42:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JOB 42:16"/>And Job lived after this a hundred and forty years, and he saw his sons and the sons of his sons, four generations. <verse eid="JOB 42:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JOB 42:17"/>And Job died, old and full of days. <verse eid="JOB 42:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="JOB 42"/>

</usx>
